1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:02,994
Hello. Great to meet you.

2
00:00:03,019 --> 00:00:04,119
(D-Day of the Wonder Coach meet-up)

3
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:06,822
Has it changed here?

4
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:09,124
Has MBC always been this nice?

5
00:00:11,156 --> 00:00:14,563
I'd been here for "Infinity Challenge"
and "Home Alone."

6
00:00:15,509 --> 00:00:17,499
Yes, I remember this place.

7
00:00:18,315 --> 00:00:19,768
We rode the elevator here.

8
00:00:20,335 --> 00:00:21,335
I remember now.

9
00:00:21,787 --> 00:00:24,120
Let's relive those memories together.

10
00:00:24,414 --> 00:00:25,974
Do we have to?

11
00:00:27,042 --> 00:00:28,456
(Yeon Koung is quite familiar with MBC.)

12
00:00:28,457 --> 00:00:30,412
Why do we have to retrace those memories?

13
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:32,715
Why are you making things awkward?

14
00:00:33,819 --> 00:00:37,375
- Have you had lunch yet?
- I had a protein shake for lunch.

15
00:00:38,055 --> 00:00:41,328
- You had a protein shake?
- After I retired,

16
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,159
I thought I should watch my weight,
so I'm taking care of myself.

17
00:00:44,508 --> 00:00:45,508
I work out too.

18
00:00:45,894 --> 00:00:49,598
(The legendary 17-year-old who debuted
as MVP of the overall championship.)

19
00:00:50,532 --> 00:00:53,034
(And after 20 years,)

20
00:00:53,435 --> 00:00:56,605
(she ended her athletic career
with another MVP title.)

21
00:00:56,805 --> 00:00:58,616
(But why is she here
after her retirement?)

22
00:00:58,616 --> 00:01:00,809
It's great to be back here at MBC.

23
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:04,780
We first met when it was still winter.

24
00:01:04,868 --> 00:01:06,081
- Yes, it was cold.
- Yes.

25
00:01:06,255 --> 00:01:09,051
It was winter
when we first met each other, and finally,

26
00:01:09,052 --> 00:01:11,387
we're here together at MBC.

27
00:01:11,776 --> 00:01:14,066
I can't believe we're doing this.
Thank you.

28
00:01:15,133 --> 00:01:17,369
- Did you read the articles?
- I did.

29
00:01:19,094 --> 00:01:22,831
(Yeon Koung reposted it
on her social media too.)

30
00:01:22,831 --> 00:01:25,005
- "A new challenge."
- Yes, "A new challenge."

31
00:01:25,385 --> 00:01:26,385
That's exactly what I said.

32
00:01:27,601 --> 00:01:30,647
Stop spying on me.
You sure are obsessed with me.

33
00:01:31,128 --> 00:01:33,242
There was a comment on that article.

34
00:01:33,654 --> 00:01:36,178
"Kim Yeon Koung is a real volleyball nut."

35
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:38,980
"She's a volleyball addict."

36
00:01:39,107 --> 00:01:42,885
You just retired from volleyball
after such a long career,

37
00:01:43,532 --> 00:01:45,398
and your first move after that...

38
00:01:45,412 --> 00:01:47,191
- is this show.
- Right.

39
00:01:47,192 --> 00:01:48,858
People are very curious about why.

40
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:50,151
To be honest,

41
00:01:51,165 --> 00:01:55,631
I've always wanted
to do something meaningful.

42
00:01:56,045 --> 00:02:00,536
I'm hoping to contribute
to the development of volleyball.

43
00:02:01,009 --> 00:02:04,748
All national team players,
both male and female,

44
00:02:04,941 --> 00:02:07,009
are facing some difficulties right now.

45
00:02:07,494 --> 00:02:09,911
So if I could help volleyball grow,

46
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:13,181
I'm willing to give it a try.

47
00:02:13,447 --> 00:02:16,459
- Do you have any specific concerns?
- Concerns?

48
00:02:18,759 --> 00:02:22,419
First, we would need
more future players...

49
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,593
who want to play
volleyball professionally.

50
00:02:25,173 --> 00:02:27,762
And we would also need a system...

51
00:02:28,112 --> 00:02:31,800
to actually train those players,
which I think we don't have at this point.

52
00:02:33,569 --> 00:02:35,178
Is it the second division?

53
00:02:35,478 --> 00:02:37,775
We'd need to establish a second division,

54
00:02:38,198 --> 00:02:40,175
so that players who cannot play
in the first division...

55
00:02:40,191 --> 00:02:43,078
can play in the second division
and have opportunities...

56
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:45,770
to grow and move up to the first division.

57
00:02:45,771 --> 00:02:47,582
We need all of those systems.

58
00:02:47,983 --> 00:02:49,284
How about baseball?

59
00:02:50,196 --> 00:02:52,096
They have a second division in baseball.

60
00:02:52,122 --> 00:02:54,356
Among the four major sports in Korea,

61
00:02:54,492 --> 00:02:57,192
volleyball is the only sport
that doesn't have a second division.

62
00:02:57,737 --> 00:02:59,961
We're in a bit of an in-between stage.
It is a professional sport,

63
00:03:00,051 --> 00:03:02,021
but we still have a long way to go.

64
00:03:02,364 --> 00:03:03,431
As a pro league.

65
00:03:04,064 --> 00:03:07,510
There's no lower team to go to,
so they end up getting dropped.

66
00:03:07,511 --> 00:03:10,763
There's no second chance.
The players are just immediately cut.

67
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:13,241
They might be good players,

68
00:03:13,409 --> 00:03:16,678
but their professional careers could
come to an end so easily.

69
00:03:17,178 --> 00:03:20,157
Players at a certain level could join
a corporate team,

70
00:03:20,157 --> 00:03:23,293
or find other ways, but as far as I know,

71
00:03:23,681 --> 00:03:26,847
we only have
very few corporate teams in Korea.

72
00:03:26,899 --> 00:03:30,833
So the players don't really
have many places to go.

73
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:34,338
We also gave it a lot of thought
after we heard that,

74
00:03:35,226 --> 00:03:37,608
and we thought you could become
a coach yourself.

75
00:03:37,609 --> 00:03:38,576
(Yeon Koung as a coach)

76
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:40,179
You could become a coach,

77
00:03:40,752 --> 00:03:42,412
and establish a team yourself...

78
00:03:42,842 --> 00:03:44,014
as a solution.

79
00:03:44,529 --> 00:03:47,014
I know. Exactly.

80
00:03:47,388 --> 00:03:49,301
You have experience as a coach, right?

81
00:03:50,004 --> 00:03:51,424
Not for long, though.

82
00:03:51,591 --> 00:03:53,987
You established the KYK Foundation,

83
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:57,094
- and your tactic was "to enjoy," right?
- Yes, enjoy.

84
00:03:57,095 --> 00:03:58,095
(Her tactic was "to enjoy.")

85
00:03:58,267 --> 00:03:59,986
That's actually my least favorite word.

86
00:04:01,226 --> 00:04:02,633
- Oh, really?
- You should give it your all.

87
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:05,965
Not a fan of pointless pep talks.
Every play should have...

88
00:04:06,146 --> 00:04:07,695
a real tactic and strategy.

89
00:04:07,934 --> 00:04:10,975
There should be a reason for a tactic,

90
00:04:11,288 --> 00:04:14,453
so the players can actually put
it into action. Pep talks come after that.

91
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:16,613
But I'd hate to just be like,

92
00:04:17,253 --> 00:04:19,345
"You feeling alright today?
Had a big meal?"

93
00:04:20,239 --> 00:04:22,086
"Ate plenty of eel?"

94
00:04:22,505 --> 00:04:24,955
"All that eel should give you some power.
Come on!"

95
00:04:25,118 --> 00:04:27,691
"Let's do this!" That's just not my thing.

96
00:04:28,311 --> 00:04:31,328
Not really a fan of that.
You do need that sometimes,

97
00:04:31,397 --> 00:04:34,657
but I'd prefer to have a strategy
that actually makes sense.

98
00:04:34,824 --> 00:04:36,470
Setting up real, meaningful tactics...

99
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,003
is probably the way I'm going to do it.

100
00:04:39,177 --> 00:04:42,262
- You already gave it so much thought.
- You think so?

101
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:44,575
You already thought things through.

102
00:04:44,962 --> 00:04:46,710
Well, I couldn't just sleep all day.

103
00:04:46,710 --> 00:04:49,680
I had to get prepared,
so I gave it some thought.

104
00:04:49,701 --> 00:04:53,250
Anyway, we thought it would be great
for you to start a team.

105
00:04:53,787 --> 00:04:55,986
And our ultimate goal is...

106
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:58,022
to become the eighth pro team
in the league.

107
00:04:58,026 --> 00:05:00,290
(The eighth pro team in the league)

108
00:05:00,666 --> 00:05:01,666
Excuse me?

109
00:05:04,196 --> 00:05:06,997
- That's our goal?
- Yes, we decided to go with that.

110
00:05:07,343 --> 00:05:09,634
- But we can't create the second division,
- Yes, of course.

111
00:05:09,682 --> 00:05:13,237
so maybe we could build a team that could
lead to a second division one day.

112
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:16,073
(Currently, there are seven pro teams
in the Korean Women's Volleyball League.)

113
00:05:17,584 --> 00:05:21,888
(Could Yeon Koung's team's name stand
next to them?)

114
00:05:22,075 --> 00:05:23,805
This is way bigger than I thought.

115
00:05:25,947 --> 00:05:28,009
The eighth pro team.
You think it's doable?

116
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:29,410
I think it is.

117
00:05:29,927 --> 00:05:32,948
Coach Yeon Koung, you can
totally achieve that.

118
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,147
Pardon?

119
00:05:34,503 --> 00:05:35,590
Your history shows that...

120
00:05:36,083 --> 00:05:39,053
you've always taken bottom-ranked teams
and made them into champions.

121
00:05:39,336 --> 00:05:42,057
Your record is unbelievable.

122
00:05:42,362 --> 00:05:44,359
Please stop pressuring me.

123
00:05:45,995 --> 00:05:49,915
- I mean, I know this is a show.
- You turned the weakest team in Japan...

124
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:53,535
- and got them their very first victory.
- Yes, please stop doing that.

125
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,104
- I'm sure it'll work out.
- Yes.

126
00:05:57,137 --> 00:05:58,506
Why did I always join losing teams?

127
00:05:58,507 --> 00:06:00,575
(Joking)

128
00:06:00,874 --> 00:06:03,657
I think the eighth pro team is
an achievable goal.

129
00:06:04,897 --> 00:06:05,897
(Concerned)

130
00:06:06,823 --> 00:06:08,907
To make our team the eighth pro team,

131
00:06:09,222 --> 00:06:12,911
we would need a great staff team
to support us.

132
00:06:13,308 --> 00:06:16,782
We would need three or four people
on the coaching team,

133
00:06:16,883 --> 00:06:19,059
and two to three performance analysts.

134
00:06:19,166 --> 00:06:23,818
We need a couple of managers, of course,
and four to five trainers.

135
00:06:24,138 --> 00:06:26,671
If we were to hold a tryout...

136
00:06:26,672 --> 00:06:28,257
to select the players,

137
00:06:28,258 --> 00:06:31,263
I was thinking we could recruit
between 14 and 16 people.

138
00:06:31,551 --> 00:06:33,826
We would also need a place to practice,

139
00:06:33,827 --> 00:06:35,413
a vehicle for transportation,

140
00:06:35,507 --> 00:06:37,327
a weight room,

141
00:06:37,328 --> 00:06:38,673
and a dorm...

142
00:06:38,674 --> 00:06:40,472
for as long as possible.

143
00:06:41,088 --> 00:06:43,748
If we were to go
to an overseas training camp,

144
00:06:44,161 --> 00:06:46,845
I was thinking we might need
a private plane.

145
00:06:47,328 --> 00:06:50,991
Like I said, we can start by playing
against high school champions...

146
00:06:50,996 --> 00:06:53,917
- and move on to corporate teams.
- Yes, right.

147
00:06:54,398 --> 00:06:57,303
After that, we can play against...

148
00:06:57,310 --> 00:06:59,691
the fringe pro teams. If we can beat them,

149
00:07:00,216 --> 00:07:02,995
I think that would be really great.

150
00:07:03,717 --> 00:07:04,719
I see.

151
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:05,720
Something wrong?

152
00:07:07,103 --> 00:07:08,683
He looks exhausted all of a sudden.

153
00:07:08,983 --> 00:07:10,169
- Right.
- Too much, right?

154
00:07:10,496 --> 00:07:12,904
I need this program to go well.

155
00:07:13,772 --> 00:07:15,273
I need you to do a phenomenal job.

156
00:07:15,479 --> 00:07:17,392
I'm counting on you
to get a private plane...

157
00:07:17,393 --> 00:07:19,845
and get us to go
to an overseas training camp.

158
00:07:20,112 --> 00:07:21,413
(Laughing)

159
00:07:21,576 --> 00:07:22,576
We need to enjoy!

160
00:07:24,185 --> 00:07:28,133
Or if things don't go the way we want,
we can go fill up on eel.

161
00:07:28,134 --> 00:07:29,687
(Eel can be a solution too.)

162
00:07:32,557 --> 00:07:34,392
(Coach signing in May)

163
00:07:35,601 --> 00:07:39,264
Hello, everyone.
We're finally here together.

164
00:07:39,541 --> 00:07:42,084
I've prepared a simple PowerPoint.

165
00:07:42,504 --> 00:07:46,238
My goal is to beat every team we face.

166
00:07:46,387 --> 00:07:49,080
We should also think about the tryout,

167
00:07:49,627 --> 00:07:52,992
and how we can see
as many players as possible.

168
00:07:52,993 --> 00:07:54,417
I've thought of a few ideas.

169
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:57,348
To recruit the team players...

170
00:07:58,349 --> 00:08:01,052
(The player recruitment was posted
on a social media platform.)

171
00:08:01,086 --> 00:08:03,488
(Anyone with a passion to play
on the professional stage can apply,)

172
00:08:03,512 --> 00:08:05,512
(including independent players
not under contract with a pro club,)

173
00:08:05,536 --> 00:08:07,492
(retired players,
and pro volleyball prospects.)

174
00:08:08,193 --> 00:08:11,296
(Overwhelming attention
and an outpouring of applications)

175
00:08:12,864 --> 00:08:14,632
(Among countless applicants,)

176
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:18,337
(those who were selected
had a two-day tryout.)

177
00:08:18,778 --> 00:08:24,743
We are testing players by position
to select 14 players.

178
00:08:25,543 --> 00:08:28,312
(Who will be the elite 14
to join Team Yeon Koung on this journey?)

179
00:08:29,023 --> 00:08:31,316
I see so many talented players.
I'm hopeful.

180
00:08:33,118 --> 00:08:35,520
(A few days later)

181
00:08:47,799 --> 00:08:51,102
(Team Yeon Koung is ready
to embark on its journey.)

182
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,142
(Squeaking)

183
00:08:58,676 --> 00:09:02,213
(Lee Jin, Daegu City, released in 2023)

184
00:09:03,281 --> 00:09:06,651
(Lee Na Yeon, a free agent,
retired in 2024)

185
00:09:07,185 --> 00:09:09,235
(Koo Sol, a free agent, released in 2025)

186
00:09:09,235 --> 00:09:10,532
I told you that you'd get in.

187
00:09:12,023 --> 00:09:15,159
(Setter: the conductor of the court)

188
00:09:15,794 --> 00:09:18,997
(Acts like the coach on the court,
directing the attacks)

189
00:09:19,931 --> 00:09:24,302
(They toss the ball to the hitters,
connecting it to make points.)

190
00:09:24,335 --> 00:09:26,871
(The perfect partner for the spiker)

191
00:09:27,705 --> 00:09:31,409
(Setters: Koo Sol, Lee Jin, Lee Na Yeon)

192
00:09:31,450 --> 00:09:33,678
I want to return to the pro league.

193
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:37,342
I'd played volleyball so far
to join a pro team,

194
00:09:37,476 --> 00:09:40,452
so it's disappointing
that I couldn't show all I've got.

195
00:09:40,556 --> 00:09:43,455
I still have a lot to show.

196
00:09:44,413 --> 00:09:48,026
My former team was suffering financially,

197
00:09:48,641 --> 00:09:51,190
But I'm still playing volleyball
because I like it so much.

198
00:09:51,271 --> 00:09:55,311
I really love the moment
I touch the ball as I arrive at the court.

199
00:09:56,276 --> 00:10:00,104
I'd like to join a pro team again
and learn many things.

200
00:10:04,375 --> 00:10:08,546
(Kim Na Hee, Suwon City, released in 2024)

201
00:10:09,034 --> 00:10:10,261
Look at her jersey. It's so cute.

202
00:10:10,915 --> 00:10:13,551
(Moon Myoung-Hwa, Daegu City,
released in 2024)

203
00:10:14,252 --> 00:10:18,056
(Kim Hyeon Jeong, a free agent,
released in 2025)

204
00:10:19,123 --> 00:10:22,893
(Middle Blocker: A solid wall at the net)

205
00:10:23,361 --> 00:10:26,764
(The team's gatekeeper
in charge of defense and quick attacks)

206
00:10:27,665 --> 00:10:30,601
(Middle Blockers: Kim Hyeon Jeong,
Kim Na Hee, Moon Myoung-Hwa)

207
00:10:31,903 --> 00:10:34,572
(Choi Su Bin, free agent, retired in 2023)

208
00:10:34,872 --> 00:10:36,635
(Koo Hye In, Daegu City, released in 2025)

209
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:37,942
- So cute.
- Right.

210
00:10:39,217 --> 00:10:42,153
(Libero: The team's last line of defense)

211
00:10:43,181 --> 00:10:46,251
(They throw their bodies
to keep the ball alive)

212
00:10:47,285 --> 00:10:50,388
(Liberos: Choi Su Bin, Koo Hye In)

213
00:10:51,089 --> 00:10:54,492
(Baek Chae Rim, Suwon City,
released in 2024)

214
00:10:55,193 --> 00:10:58,663
(Han Song Hee, Pohang Sports Council,
released in 2022)

215
00:10:59,364 --> 00:11:02,538
(Enkhsoyol, Mokpo Science University,
formerly on the Mongolian national team)

216
00:11:02,539 --> 00:11:03,539
She's cute.

217
00:11:03,601 --> 00:11:06,871
(Bulgantamir, Mokpo Science University,
formerly on the Mongolian national team)

218
00:11:07,572 --> 00:11:10,208
(A Mongolian teammate
from Mokpo Science University)

219
00:11:10,815 --> 00:11:14,819
(Outside Hitter: The team's anchor)

220
00:11:15,446 --> 00:11:18,883
(An all-rounder capable
of both offense and defense)

221
00:11:20,385 --> 00:11:23,488
(Outside Hitters: Enkhsoyol, Bulgantamir,
Baek Chae Rim, Han Song Hee)

222
00:11:23,488 --> 00:11:27,140
I'm Enkhsoyol, and I'm from Mongolia.

223
00:11:27,786 --> 00:11:31,859
I'm ineligible to join both professional
and semi-professional teams...

224
00:11:32,155 --> 00:11:34,908
due to nationality issues.

225
00:11:35,039 --> 00:11:40,998
I never even imagined myself playing...

226
00:11:41,198 --> 00:11:44,490
in the Korean league,

227
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:47,957
but if things go well here, it could be
a chance to join a Korean pro team.

228
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:50,330
So I thought, "I got in!"

229
00:11:50,331 --> 00:11:52,790
"I should learn as much as I can there."

230
00:11:54,064 --> 00:11:55,929
I don't mind how intense the training is.

231
00:11:57,369 --> 00:12:00,968
I came here because I wanted to play
for a Korean pro team.

232
00:12:01,188 --> 00:12:04,795
My role model is Kim Yeon Koung.

233
00:12:05,462 --> 00:12:08,099
Do you know who the coach of this team is?

234
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:10,293
(Doesn't know)

235
00:12:10,294 --> 00:12:11,887
- It's Coach Kim Yeon Koung.
- What?

236
00:12:18,776 --> 00:12:22,546
(Choking up at the unexpected mention
of the name)

237
00:12:24,164 --> 00:12:26,818
Those are happy tears, right?

238
00:12:26,819 --> 00:12:28,753
(Being here must've been
a lifelong dream for some.)

239
00:12:29,185 --> 00:12:31,097
There she is.

240
00:12:31,355 --> 00:12:36,961
(Yoon Young In, Suwon City,
no pro-league experience)

241
00:12:37,595 --> 00:12:40,832
(Opposite spiker: The team's closer)

242
00:12:41,632 --> 00:12:44,568
(The key attacker on the right side
of the court)

243
00:12:45,369 --> 00:12:47,805
(Opposite Spiker: Yoon Young In)

244
00:12:47,987 --> 00:12:51,175
Hi, I'm Yoon Young In,
and I'm in my eighth year with Suwon City.

245
00:12:51,494 --> 00:12:54,120
Ever since my school days,
I've had a dream,

246
00:12:54,213 --> 00:12:57,648
which is to go pro.

247
00:12:58,245 --> 00:13:01,718
In my heart, I sometimes wondered...

248
00:13:01,825 --> 00:13:04,191
what it would be like to play
on the professional stage.

249
00:13:04,878 --> 00:13:08,693
This is such a precious opportunity.

250
00:13:08,706 --> 00:13:11,229
It's my dream
and someone else's dream as well,

251
00:13:11,337 --> 00:13:14,084
so I don't want to take it lightly.

252
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:17,168
I hope it's a chance
for me to make a fresh start.

253
00:13:19,259 --> 00:13:20,392
Gosh.

254
00:13:20,398 --> 00:13:23,908
(They all came here
with a desperate dream.)

255
00:13:24,759 --> 00:13:26,511
Who'll take this last spot?

256
00:13:26,512 --> 00:13:27,945
(There's only one spot left.)

257
00:13:28,579 --> 00:13:31,115
(Who will be the final piece
to complete the team?)

258
00:13:33,168 --> 00:13:36,838
(All cheering)

259
00:13:39,257 --> 00:13:41,257
(Pyo Seung Ju, free agent,
retired in 2025)

260
00:13:41,257 --> 00:13:42,588
You're all here.

261
00:13:43,284 --> 00:13:44,671
The star always comes last.

262
00:13:44,797 --> 00:13:46,331
You look so cool.

263
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:49,188
- Hi.
- Hello.

264
00:13:49,262 --> 00:13:51,998
(She's back after five months.)

265
00:13:55,567 --> 00:13:59,938
(Her class never fades.)

266
00:14:00,210 --> 00:14:02,457
She runs the game differently.

267
00:14:02,937 --> 00:14:06,412
She can join a pro team
and the national team any time,

268
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:08,848
so I was shocked to see her here.

269
00:14:09,795 --> 00:14:10,650
They're all here.

270
00:14:11,317 --> 00:14:13,686
(Successfully recruited 14 elite players.)

271
00:14:14,921 --> 00:14:16,890
(But the door opens again!)

272
00:14:19,375 --> 00:14:20,868
What?

273
00:14:24,964 --> 00:14:28,134
(Boo Seung Kwan, the team manager)

274
00:14:29,408 --> 00:14:32,307
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello!

275
00:14:33,653 --> 00:14:37,443
(Fascinated by each other)

276
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,879
- Nice to meet you.
- Hi.

277
00:14:41,614 --> 00:14:44,016
(The world-class idol singer)

278
00:14:44,450 --> 00:14:47,286
(The main vocalist of SEVENTEEN,
Seung Kwan)

279
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:51,624
I've been a fan of V-League for 20 years.

280
00:14:52,064 --> 00:14:55,703
I've been a CheongKwanJang Red Sparks fan
since the league's foundation in 2005.

281
00:14:56,676 --> 00:15:00,035
People think I'm just a fan
of the Red Sparks,

282
00:15:00,055 --> 00:15:02,602
but I love volleyball itself. Last year,

283
00:15:02,708 --> 00:15:05,294
- I watched almost every game.
- Really?

284
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:08,197
I watched many matches on TV.

285
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:10,700
I've even made some friends
who love volleyball too.

286
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:15,048
I also know the play styles and strengths
of the other teams well.

287
00:15:15,303 --> 00:15:19,485
I probably know every player
who has ever played in the pro league.

288
00:15:20,155 --> 00:15:23,305
I see so many familiar faces now,

289
00:15:23,572 --> 00:15:26,993
and seeing Seung Ju here
feels different...

290
00:15:27,278 --> 00:15:30,284
since she played until last year.

291
00:15:31,117 --> 00:15:34,636
There's also Na Yeon, and Jin is here too.

292
00:15:34,716 --> 00:15:38,583
I see Su Bin, Na Hee,

293
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:42,675
and Sol too. There you are, Myoung-Hwa.

294
00:15:42,982 --> 00:15:46,118
Thank you for recognizing me.

295
00:15:46,765 --> 00:15:50,858
You're all like celebrities to me.

296
00:15:51,211 --> 00:15:53,519
As the manager of this team,

297
00:15:53,751 --> 00:15:56,437
I will bring vitality to everyone.

298
00:15:57,256 --> 00:15:58,858
(So reliable)

299
00:15:58,871 --> 00:16:01,790
Now, let's welcome the coaching staff!

300
00:16:01,791 --> 00:16:04,230
(The coaching staff enters)

301
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:11,604
(Living up to the rookie coach's ambition)

302
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:15,174
(All entering together)

303
00:16:16,375 --> 00:16:19,278
(In charge of coaching and training)

304
00:16:19,759 --> 00:16:23,249
Meet coaches Kim Tae Young, Lee Yeon Ju,
and Jeong Wu Seong.

305
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:24,717
(Kim Tae Young,
Lee Yeon Ju, Jeong Wu Seong)

306
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:27,281
(In charge of opponent analysis
and strategy planning)

307
00:16:27,308 --> 00:16:30,298
Now for the performance analysts.
Welcome Nam Ye Rin and Chae Sang Min.

308
00:16:30,299 --> 00:16:31,925
(Nam Ye Rin, Chae Sang Min)

309
00:16:32,583 --> 00:16:36,696
I'm in charge of the players' fitness.
I handle strength training,

310
00:16:36,697 --> 00:16:40,724
injury management, and rehabilitation.

311
00:16:41,062 --> 00:16:44,804
Here are trainers Lee Sang Hwa,
Jeong Jong Il, and Park Ye Jin.

312
00:16:44,805 --> 00:16:46,439
(Lee Sang Hwa, Jeong Jong Il, Park Ye Jin)

313
00:16:47,388 --> 00:16:51,727
I've worked with Yeon Koung
since her first year on a pro team.

314
00:16:53,304 --> 00:16:59,704
(He looked after her for 20 years
from 2005 to 2025.)

315
00:17:00,471 --> 00:17:04,804
We were in the same team
for 20 years until she retired.

316
00:17:05,871 --> 00:17:07,771
(29 years of experience)

317
00:17:08,037 --> 00:17:09,904
(30 years of experience)

318
00:17:10,437 --> 00:17:12,704
(The two trainers have been close
for 30 years.)

319
00:17:13,204 --> 00:17:14,504
(Yeon Koung's best coaching staff)

320
00:17:14,504 --> 00:17:15,904
Next up.

321
00:17:16,271 --> 00:17:18,637
She's the leader who will guide this team.

322
00:17:19,137 --> 00:17:21,837
Coach Kim Yeon Koung, please enter.

323
00:17:24,095 --> 00:17:25,929
After 20 years as an athlete,

324
00:17:27,862 --> 00:17:30,429
she is back as a new coach.

325
00:17:31,962 --> 00:17:35,495
Coach Kim Yeon Koung is entering
from the second floor!

326
00:17:41,629 --> 00:17:43,662
- Awesome!
- She's so cool.

327
00:17:43,662 --> 00:17:47,262
(Kim Yeon Koung, the new coach)

328
00:17:47,762 --> 00:17:49,695
(She will lead 14 athletes...)

329
00:17:49,695 --> 00:17:51,529
- So cool.
- I like her!

330
00:17:52,195 --> 00:17:57,429
(as a new coach.)

331
00:17:57,462 --> 00:17:59,729
She's really charismatic.

332
00:18:04,429 --> 00:18:05,829
(A little embarrassed)

333
00:18:05,829 --> 00:18:06,995
Check out her aura.

334
00:18:08,729 --> 00:18:10,762
This isn't easy.

335
00:18:11,195 --> 00:18:12,695
I can't see her face.

336
00:18:13,095 --> 00:18:14,462
She's literally glowing.

337
00:18:14,462 --> 00:18:16,129
(Her first steps as a coach)

338
00:18:16,129 --> 00:18:17,129
This is not an easy task.

339
00:18:18,995 --> 00:18:20,395
(The legendary volleyball empress)

340
00:18:20,395 --> 00:18:23,229
(A new head coach)

341
00:18:27,662 --> 00:18:32,062
We have the players, the head coach,
and the coaching staff...

342
00:18:32,262 --> 00:18:34,462
all gathered as a team.

343
00:18:34,462 --> 00:18:36,029
Now that the team is complete,

344
00:18:36,029 --> 00:18:39,529
we'll reveal the name of our team.

345
00:18:40,429 --> 00:18:41,595
Let's see what it is!

346
00:18:45,929 --> 00:18:48,062
The video turned out great, right?

347
00:18:50,562 --> 00:18:51,929
I got goosebumps.

348
00:18:54,529 --> 00:18:57,862
Our players may be underdogs for now,

349
00:18:59,895 --> 00:19:02,829
but they will rise to be a wonder.

350
00:19:03,695 --> 00:19:06,129
They're the Victorious Wonder Dogs.

351
00:19:06,129 --> 00:19:08,595
(The Victorious Wonder Dogs)

352
00:19:12,129 --> 00:19:13,629
Do you like the name, Coach?

353
00:19:14,029 --> 00:19:16,295
I love the logo.

354
00:19:16,829 --> 00:19:21,095
If you look closely,
it's in the shape of a volleyball.

355
00:19:21,329 --> 00:19:23,195
And they added an element of underdogs...

356
00:19:23,195 --> 00:19:26,529
by combining a dog's image
with the volleyball.

357
00:19:26,995 --> 00:19:28,162
That's the part I like about it.

358
00:19:28,162 --> 00:19:31,762
I even got goosebumps
when I looked at the logo.

359
00:19:31,762 --> 00:19:33,629
- You got goosebumps.
- Yeah, I did.

360
00:19:34,129 --> 00:19:37,162
And so the founding ceremony will...

361
00:19:37,162 --> 00:19:38,195
What?

362
00:19:38,995 --> 00:19:39,995
What?

363
00:19:57,601 --> 00:19:58,962
(Salary per team,
Pro team: 3,000,000 dollars)

364
00:19:58,962 --> 00:19:59,962
What's that?

365
00:20:03,395 --> 00:20:04,462
(Wonder Dogs: 200,000 dollars)

366
00:20:04,495 --> 00:20:05,995
(Total salaries per team)

367
00:20:05,995 --> 00:20:07,895
(3 million dollars vs. 200,000 dollars)

368
00:20:26,862 --> 00:20:28,462
(Top Seven Pro Female Players
with the Highest Salaries)

369
00:20:28,462 --> 00:20:30,195
(Lee Da Hyeon: 550,000 dollars)

370
00:20:30,795 --> 00:20:33,929
(Lee Da Hyeon's draftmate
from Jungang Girls' High School)

371
00:20:35,595 --> 00:20:39,295
(Lee Da Hyeon's draftmate)

372
00:20:40,395 --> 00:20:41,862
(Bae Yu Na: 550,000 dollars)

373
00:20:41,862 --> 00:20:43,329
(Jeong Ji Yun: 650,000 dollars)

374
00:20:43,329 --> 00:20:46,395
(Lee So Young: 700,000 dollars)

375
00:20:46,395 --> 00:20:49,962
(Lee So Young's draftmate)

376
00:20:50,495 --> 00:20:53,029
(Park Jeong Ah: 775,000 dollars)

377
00:20:53,429 --> 00:20:57,695
(Park Jeong Ah's draftmates)

378
00:20:57,729 --> 00:20:59,962
(Kang So Hwi: 800,000 dollars)

379
00:20:59,962 --> 00:21:02,195
(Yang Hyo Jin: 800,000 dollars)

380
00:21:02,862 --> 00:21:07,162
An athlete's skill is reflected
in their salary.

381
00:21:11,695 --> 00:21:16,262
The following is a ranking table
of salaries based on FD ratings.

382
00:21:18,262 --> 00:21:20,162
(Rank A: 100,000 dollars or more,
Rank B: less than 100,000 dollars)

383
00:21:20,162 --> 00:21:21,895
(Rank C: less than 50,000 dollars,
Rank F: less than 20,000 dollars)

384
00:21:21,929 --> 00:21:24,829
Salaries represent skills.

385
00:21:26,395 --> 00:21:32,462
We will now reveal the salary ratings
of the Wonder Dogs players.

386
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:38,360
(Only the income earned
as a volleyball player is included.)

387
00:21:41,698 --> 00:21:43,580
(Current Salary Rating, Koo Sol)

388
00:21:44,227 --> 00:21:47,794
(Koo Sol)

389
00:21:48,694 --> 00:21:53,827
(Koo Sol: F)

390
00:22:06,027 --> 00:22:07,494
(Lee Na Yeon)

391
00:22:07,727 --> 00:22:10,194
(Lee Na Yeon)

392
00:22:10,327 --> 00:22:13,627
We heard you gave up 160,000 dollars...

393
00:22:13,794 --> 00:22:16,760
and retired in less than a year
of your contract.

394
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:18,127
I guess I ran away.

395
00:22:18,127 --> 00:22:21,294
I got the yips while playing.

396
00:22:21,794 --> 00:22:24,227
Even when I was just holding the ball,

397
00:22:24,327 --> 00:22:28,494
I couldn't breathe
and felt like my whole hand was twisting.

398
00:22:28,627 --> 00:22:32,694
But time didn't wait for me
to overcome that and get back in shape.

399
00:22:32,694 --> 00:22:35,594
So I eventually fell behind others.

400
00:22:36,727 --> 00:22:39,760
I wanted to play volleyball.

401
00:22:40,127 --> 00:22:42,760
I used to love it so much.

402
00:22:43,027 --> 00:22:44,294
It's a shame.

403
00:22:44,294 --> 00:22:46,794
I wish I could enjoy playing
volleyball again like I used to.

404
00:22:47,827 --> 00:22:50,560
(Lee Na Yeon: F)

405
00:22:51,060 --> 00:22:53,294
(Lee Jin)

406
00:22:54,127 --> 00:22:55,960
(Lee Jin: C)

407
00:22:59,660 --> 00:23:01,460
(Kim Na Hee: C)

408
00:23:01,727 --> 00:23:03,460
(Kim Na Hee)

409
00:23:03,494 --> 00:23:05,160
(Yoon Young In: C)

410
00:23:05,194 --> 00:23:07,060
(Yoon Young In)

411
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:08,694
(Baek Chae Rim: C)

412
00:23:08,727 --> 00:23:10,427
(Baek Chae Rim)

413
00:23:10,427 --> 00:23:11,460
(Moon Myoung-Hwa: C)

414
00:23:11,460 --> 00:23:12,527
(Han Song Hee: C)

415
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:13,627
(Moon Myoung-Hwa)

416
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:15,027
(Han Song Hee)

417
00:23:15,327 --> 00:23:17,160
(Pyo Seung Ju)

418
00:23:17,494 --> 00:23:19,260
(Pyo Seung Ju)

419
00:23:22,027 --> 00:23:24,260
(Pyo Seung Ju: F)

420
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:37,727
(Choi Su Bin: F)

421
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:40,027
(Koo Hye In: C)

422
00:23:40,060 --> 00:23:42,194
(Bulgantamir: F)

423
00:23:42,227 --> 00:23:44,060
(Enkhsoyol: F)

424
00:23:44,094 --> 00:23:45,860
(Kim Hyeon Jeong: F)

425
00:23:46,094 --> 00:23:49,860
(Kim Hyeon Jeong)

426
00:23:55,194 --> 00:23:57,127
I was being thrown to the bottom.

427
00:23:57,127 --> 00:23:59,627
It felt like they were saying,
"You belong down there."

428
00:23:59,627 --> 00:24:00,994
So I didn't feel great.

429
00:24:03,227 --> 00:24:05,027
Yet, it motivated me a lot.

430
00:24:05,427 --> 00:24:06,494
Looking back,

431
00:24:06,894 --> 00:24:09,827
I guess that gave me more of a reason
to try harder here.

432
00:24:10,494 --> 00:24:13,494
(Do you think
they're getting fair salaries?)

433
00:24:14,094 --> 00:24:15,394
Of course not.

434
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:21,360
They're competitive enough to join
and play for a pro team.

435
00:24:21,594 --> 00:24:25,627
I think they just weren't given a chance.

436
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:27,860
I believe...

437
00:24:28,453 --> 00:24:33,487
that we should increase their salaries
to be close to those of the pro teams.

438
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:35,494
I have to try.

439
00:24:40,227 --> 00:24:43,994
(We interviewed volleyball personnel
to evaluate Wonder Dogs objectively.)

440
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:52,294
(Cha Sang Hyun, former head coach
of KIXX Volleyball Club)

441
00:24:52,794 --> 00:24:55,827
(Lee Jung Chul, former head coach
of Altos Volleyball Club)

442
00:24:56,760 --> 00:25:00,194
(Song Hyun Il, journalist
for volleyball magazine)

443
00:25:00,927 --> 00:25:04,327
(Kim Jeong Ah, performance analyst
of the youth national team)

444
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:08,527
We must evaluate
their performance objectively.

445
00:25:09,627 --> 00:25:12,994
(Lee Na Yeon)

446
00:25:17,594 --> 00:25:19,094
During her prime,

447
00:25:19,194 --> 00:25:22,827
she was even viewed
as the next generation's national athlete.

448
00:25:22,994 --> 00:25:25,294
We can all agree on her skills.

449
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:28,294
Na Yeon is skillful enough.

450
00:25:28,560 --> 00:25:31,027
If we're talking about her mental state,

451
00:25:31,327 --> 00:25:34,460
she fails to meet our expectations of her.

452
00:25:34,794 --> 00:25:38,060
She struggled to maintain
composure on the court,

453
00:25:38,127 --> 00:25:39,860
which was a serious issue.

454
00:25:39,994 --> 00:25:43,260
The same problems
with her mental state might happen again.

455
00:25:43,827 --> 00:25:45,794
We have many concerns about her.

456
00:25:50,766 --> 00:25:52,832
(Lee Jin)

457
00:25:55,827 --> 00:25:59,594
If we consider ball speed only
in regard to her tossing skill,

458
00:25:59,894 --> 00:26:02,427
she's one of the top players.

459
00:26:02,460 --> 00:26:04,260
- She tosses really fast.
- It's very quick.

460
00:26:04,294 --> 00:26:06,160
- Doesn't she also have good showmanship?
- Yes, she does.

461
00:26:06,260 --> 00:26:10,260
She can gain popularity with the public
and is also skilled.

462
00:26:10,794 --> 00:26:15,394
But she was often talked about
because of her looks.

463
00:26:16,060 --> 00:26:20,227
She received too much attention
despite her young age.

464
00:26:20,894 --> 00:26:24,560
So she mistook her fame for her skills.

465
00:26:24,627 --> 00:26:26,327
- That's my opinion.
- I agree.

466
00:26:28,694 --> 00:26:30,060
That breaks my heart.

467
00:26:37,094 --> 00:26:39,860
(What was it like
to watch your evaluation video?)

468
00:26:49,060 --> 00:26:50,060
I said I wouldn't cry.

469
00:26:58,134 --> 00:27:01,415
Many people said that about me
when I was on a pro team.

470
00:27:02,061 --> 00:27:06,120
Because a lot of people judge us.

471
00:27:06,633 --> 00:27:08,585
I didn't even have many chances
to get on the court,

472
00:27:08,879 --> 00:27:11,392
so people said
I only cared about my looks.

473
00:27:15,852 --> 00:27:17,587
My feelings were hurt.

474
00:27:20,657 --> 00:27:22,893
(Pyo Seung Ju)

475
00:27:26,224 --> 00:27:28,031
Why is this player here?

476
00:27:31,423 --> 00:27:34,356
- Her skills look flawless.
- Yes, absolutely.

477
00:27:34,570 --> 00:27:38,374
- In terms of skill, she's way ahead.
- Well, to be exact,

478
00:27:39,162 --> 00:27:41,577
she used to be way ahead.

479
00:27:42,542 --> 00:27:45,482
Whether it was her decision or not,

480
00:27:46,448 --> 00:27:48,785
she did retire suddenly.

481
00:27:49,321 --> 00:27:52,189
If all seven pro teams really consider
you a key player,

482
00:27:52,434 --> 00:27:55,460
you'd be at the top of the pyramid.
But for the players...

483
00:27:55,547 --> 00:27:57,560
whose abilities are just so-so,

484
00:27:57,896 --> 00:28:00,763
they get stuck somewhere in between.

485
00:28:01,016 --> 00:28:02,795
They're just stuck in the middle.

486
00:28:03,122 --> 00:28:06,836
Other teams don't desperately want her.

487
00:28:06,837 --> 00:28:09,606
(Not an attractive pick)

488
00:28:13,584 --> 00:28:15,131
They're just saying
whatever comes to mind.

489
00:28:23,498 --> 00:28:24,975
During my entire volleyball career,

490
00:28:25,502 --> 00:28:28,220
I never thought I was a good player.

491
00:28:28,234 --> 00:28:32,028
I always felt like I wasn't good enough.
Just run-of-the-mill.

492
00:28:33,314 --> 00:28:34,797
I've always thought that,

493
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:39,502
and then that was exactly
how I was evaluated as an FA.

494
00:28:40,212 --> 00:28:41,971
Even I think that...

495
00:28:42,259 --> 00:28:44,474
if I were a really good player,

496
00:28:44,712 --> 00:28:47,376
I would've been able to join another team.

497
00:28:47,725 --> 00:28:50,938
So I wrote in my retirement letter that,
even though it wasn't very flashy,

498
00:28:51,350 --> 00:28:53,557
I want to be remembered
as a player who always did her best.

499
00:28:53,570 --> 00:28:56,219
("My career may not have been glamorous,
but I've always worked hard.")

500
00:28:56,410 --> 00:28:58,554
Of course, it's annoying and frustrating,

501
00:28:58,883 --> 00:29:00,924
but that's a label I can't shake off.

502
00:29:01,396 --> 00:29:03,693
I actually accept that.

503
00:29:07,948 --> 00:29:10,428
Here comes Coach Cha's sore spot.

504
00:29:11,001 --> 00:29:11,824
Moon Myoung-Hwa.

505
00:29:12,368 --> 00:29:15,605
(Moon Myoung-Hwa)

506
00:29:16,044 --> 00:29:18,523
That name makes me want a drink.

507
00:29:21,210 --> 00:29:25,222
I know better than anyone that she is...

508
00:29:25,356 --> 00:29:29,765
smart, intelligent, and hard-working.
But she's slow.

509
00:29:31,001 --> 00:29:34,090
I once said to a trainer
that if they could make her faster,

510
00:29:34,574 --> 00:29:39,195
I would do whatever it takes
to put them at the top of the pyramid.

511
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:42,619
- I begged them to make her faster.
- But they couldn't, right?

512
00:29:42,766 --> 00:29:44,367
Even personalized training failed.

513
00:29:44,913 --> 00:29:48,885
I can't even criticize her.
She works harder than anyone.

514
00:29:49,079 --> 00:29:50,372
But she's slow.

515
00:29:51,108 --> 00:29:55,141
There's nothing bad you can say about her.
She works so hard, but she's slow.

516
00:29:55,142 --> 00:29:57,844
(She's just slow.)

517
00:29:57,877 --> 00:29:59,946
(Kim Na Hee)

518
00:30:01,236 --> 00:30:03,686
She's 36 years old? Considering her age,

519
00:30:03,726 --> 00:30:06,982
- being on the court wouldn't be easy.
- It could be risky.

520
00:30:07,622 --> 00:30:11,291
To begin with, she was never recruited
into a pro team.

521
00:30:11,908 --> 00:30:14,627
She doesn't have the physical strength
to last on the court.

522
00:30:15,671 --> 00:30:18,431
She's just too short to join a pro team.

523
00:30:18,958 --> 00:30:22,201
- She can't even score on a free ball.
- Right, not even an easy one.

524
00:30:22,643 --> 00:30:24,503
She doesn't have a standout skill.

525
00:30:25,203 --> 00:30:28,689
Apart from her height, I don't know
what other advantages she has.

526
00:30:33,646 --> 00:30:34,321
Oh, gosh.

527
00:30:35,088 --> 00:30:36,088
Here she is.

528
00:30:36,568 --> 00:30:38,117
- Oh, dear.
- Here she is.

529
00:30:42,255 --> 00:30:45,024
(Coach Kim Yeon Koung)

530
00:30:49,899 --> 00:30:51,998
They're evaluating Coach Yeon Koung?

531
00:30:53,791 --> 00:30:55,064
I bet they'll have nothing to say.

532
00:30:55,351 --> 00:30:56,898
What would they even say?

533
00:30:58,050 --> 00:31:02,105
If they say something bad,
I'm going to call them right up.

534
00:31:05,396 --> 00:31:07,149
- Go ahead, Coach.
- Yes, you first.

535
00:31:07,729 --> 00:31:09,348
Why are you throwing me under the bus?

536
00:31:09,412 --> 00:31:11,547
(Pushing each other to go first)

537
00:31:15,427 --> 00:31:19,321
Well, this is a candid assessment session.

538
00:31:20,804 --> 00:31:21,804
What do you think, Coach?

539
00:31:22,659 --> 00:31:24,127
Well...

540
00:31:24,727 --> 00:31:25,328
(Deep breath)

541
00:31:25,723 --> 00:31:28,397
The job of a player and a coach...

542
00:31:28,813 --> 00:31:30,620
are completely different.

543
00:31:30,946 --> 00:31:32,425
Well, I know that.

544
00:31:33,325 --> 00:31:39,174
They say that a good player doesn't
necessarily make a good coach.

545
00:31:39,661 --> 00:31:43,347
If she's seeing this as just another show,
she's deeply mistaken.

546
00:31:43,587 --> 00:31:46,282
If she can be a real coach and a mentor,

547
00:31:46,594 --> 00:31:48,146
I'm not quite sure yet.

548
00:31:48,446 --> 00:31:51,153
If her goal is to be the real leader
of this team,

549
00:31:51,380 --> 00:31:52,753
I hope she'll be really serious.

550
00:31:53,492 --> 00:31:54,690
With all her heart.

551
00:31:55,942 --> 00:31:59,752
For the many fans who love volleyball,

552
00:32:00,139 --> 00:32:01,731
I hope she's really serious about this.

553
00:32:02,098 --> 00:32:04,834
(The Wonder Dogs' odds of winning)

554
00:32:05,198 --> 00:32:09,472
Honestly, I'm not even expecting
50 percent.

555
00:32:09,721 --> 00:32:11,468
Even one or two wins won't be easy.

556
00:32:11,648 --> 00:32:13,076
It's all up to how they prepare
themselves.

557
00:32:20,159 --> 00:32:21,159
Coach Yeon Koung,

558
00:32:23,239 --> 00:32:24,239
What do you think?

559
00:32:24,625 --> 00:32:27,757
You heard the evaluations
of volleyball experts.

560
00:32:28,664 --> 00:32:32,361
I think we should evaluate
those experts as well.

561
00:32:33,257 --> 00:32:35,531
Whether I'm a real leader or not?

562
00:32:35,657 --> 00:32:38,834
I'm not even sure they know enough
to be asking that question.

563
00:32:39,363 --> 00:32:41,137
- Feels so good to hear that.
- As for our players,

564
00:32:41,330 --> 00:32:43,840
I'm sure they have
their strengths and weaknesses.

565
00:32:45,742 --> 00:32:46,776
(Staring)

566
00:32:47,742 --> 00:32:49,908
Myoung-Hwa, you're too slow.

567
00:32:49,909 --> 00:32:54,062
- But I'm a real speedster.
- You're too slow, Myoung-Hwa.

568
00:32:54,063 --> 00:32:55,051
(Let's find out...)

569
00:32:55,985 --> 00:32:58,454
(how she really felt
about the evaluation.)

570
00:32:58,818 --> 00:33:00,356
I guess I'm a fake leader.

571
00:33:00,525 --> 00:33:02,235
I guess they don't count it
if it's a variety show.

572
00:33:03,088 --> 00:33:03,714
(Are you upset?)

573
00:33:03,715 --> 00:33:05,295
No, of course not.

574
00:33:05,574 --> 00:33:08,193
I'm not even a real leader, you know.

575
00:33:08,867 --> 00:33:09,867
- Right.
- I'm okay.

576
00:33:09,868 --> 00:33:10,967
(Clearly upset)

577
00:33:11,427 --> 00:33:15,738
Players of our team,
the Victorious Wonder Dogs, are underdogs.

578
00:33:20,476 --> 00:33:23,631
The ultimate goal
of the Victorious Wonder Dogs is...

579
00:33:24,981 --> 00:33:26,684
(The eighth pro team)

580
00:33:26,684 --> 00:33:28,217
to make the eighth pro team in the league.

581
00:33:33,563 --> 00:33:37,460
Until we find someone
who wants to be a team owner,

582
00:33:37,955 --> 00:33:41,523
you have to survive by proving your worth.

583
00:33:43,342 --> 00:33:44,600
This season...

584
00:33:44,962 --> 00:33:48,637
is going to be your first test
toward our goal.

585
00:33:50,852 --> 00:33:54,978
We're going to play against seven teams.

586
00:33:57,278 --> 00:33:58,278
A pro team.

587
00:34:00,730 --> 00:34:01,730
A corporate league champion.

588
00:34:03,103 --> 00:34:04,103
A university champion.

589
00:34:05,489 --> 00:34:06,489
A girls' high school champion.

590
00:34:08,132 --> 00:34:09,725
A Japanese high school champion.

591
00:34:12,711 --> 00:34:13,711
A pro runner-up team.

592
00:34:16,161 --> 00:34:17,266
And lastly,

593
00:34:19,648 --> 00:34:21,137
A pro league overall champion.

594
00:34:24,507 --> 00:34:28,144
(The seven teams the Wonder Dogs will
play against)

595
00:34:31,236 --> 00:34:33,149
You will play against these seven teams,

596
00:34:35,401 --> 00:34:37,386
and must secure more wins than losses.

597
00:34:38,538 --> 00:34:40,658
If you lose more than three games,

598
00:34:41,385 --> 00:34:43,326
the Victorious Wonder Dogs...

599
00:34:45,340 --> 00:34:46,562
will shut down.

600
00:34:57,272 --> 00:34:59,764
The first team the Wonder Dogs...

601
00:35:00,190 --> 00:35:01,610
will play against...

602
00:35:02,171 --> 00:35:03,171
will now be revealed.

603
00:35:06,384 --> 00:35:08,084
Our first opponent is...

604
00:35:10,083 --> 00:35:11,083
the girls' high school champion.

605
00:35:16,553 --> 00:35:17,860
Jeonju Geunyoung Girls' High School.

606
00:35:20,529 --> 00:35:23,599
(Their volleyball team was founded
in 1975,)

607
00:35:24,166 --> 00:35:27,803
(and they are currently the number one
girls' high school volleyball team.)

608
00:35:28,646 --> 00:35:31,415
(Their players were even chosen...)

609
00:35:31,916 --> 00:35:34,252
(as the first overall selections
in the 2025 draft.)

610
00:35:34,285 --> 00:35:35,753
(After the legendary players,
Jang Yoon Hee,)

611
00:35:35,753 --> 00:35:37,255
(Lee So Young,)

612
00:35:37,895 --> 00:35:40,376
(and many other rising stars...)

613
00:35:40,822 --> 00:35:43,158
(are taking over the court.)

614
00:35:43,217 --> 00:35:45,616
I'm Choi Wu Young, the chief coach
of Jeonju Geunyoung Girls' High School.

615
00:35:45,789 --> 00:35:46,936
I'm Coach Yang Cheol Ho.

616
00:35:47,489 --> 00:35:49,876
Geunyoung Girls' High has two coaches,

617
00:35:50,036 --> 00:35:51,334
and thus, our strength is double.

618
00:35:51,942 --> 00:35:55,470
The difference between 47 years
of coaching experience and none is huge.

619
00:35:56,239 --> 00:35:58,671
Now that she's about to make
her debut as a coach,

620
00:35:58,852 --> 00:36:01,587
I think she needs to learn more.

621
00:36:01,934 --> 00:36:04,008
You can't ignore years of experience.

622
00:36:08,376 --> 00:36:10,196
Coach Kim's team hasn't...

623
00:36:10,270 --> 00:36:12,620
had enough time to build fitness...

624
00:36:12,769 --> 00:36:14,655
and coordination,

625
00:36:14,995 --> 00:36:17,224
but we've been training...

626
00:36:17,342 --> 00:36:18,994
and working on teamwork consistently.

627
00:36:19,075 --> 00:36:21,028
Our strength lies in solid fundamentals.

628
00:36:21,075 --> 00:36:23,794
Our players have agility,
make good decisions,

629
00:36:23,994 --> 00:36:25,866
and know how to read games.

630
00:36:28,227 --> 00:36:31,105
We've played
against pro and semi-pro teams,

631
00:36:31,194 --> 00:36:35,142
so taking on retired players
should be doable.

632
00:36:37,590 --> 00:36:38,709
We won't lose.

633
00:36:39,216 --> 00:36:43,139
- With our high fitness, we'll beat them.
- We'll win.

634
00:36:52,058 --> 00:36:53,784
The match
against Jeonju Geunyoung Girls' High...

635
00:36:54,650 --> 00:36:56,864
will be held next Thursday.

636
00:37:02,232 --> 00:37:03,404
We actually don't have enough time.

637
00:37:04,009 --> 00:37:05,120
We're in trouble.

638
00:37:05,664 --> 00:37:07,042
Geunyoung Girls' High...

639
00:37:08,342 --> 00:37:10,144
(Mental breakdown)

640
00:37:10,268 --> 00:37:12,853
They're definitely not an easy team,

641
00:37:14,307 --> 00:37:16,383
so I thought I should give it my all.

642
00:37:16,546 --> 00:37:17,405
We have to win.

643
00:37:17,530 --> 00:37:21,055
I think we should focus on winning for now
and worry about the rest later.

644
00:37:21,269 --> 00:37:24,081
I need to implement my style of volleyball
with the team quickly...

645
00:37:24,643 --> 00:37:26,327
and run the game.

646
00:37:26,602 --> 00:37:30,231
I'll prepare well
to build the team properly.

647
00:37:31,198 --> 00:37:36,437
(Episode 1, "Real Coach Kim Yeon Koung")

648
00:37:36,438 --> 00:37:38,790
(Ansan, Gyeonggi-do)

649
00:37:38,791 --> 00:37:41,174
It feels strange
to make my coaching debut in my hometown.

650
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:46,373
- Did everyone sleep well yesterday?
- Yes.

651
00:37:46,374 --> 00:37:48,632
Let's take a look at the strategy
of Geunyoung Girls' High School.

652
00:37:48,782 --> 00:37:51,304
(Wonder Dogs' Training Schedule,
Morning: video meeting)

653
00:37:51,305 --> 00:37:53,917
I prefer analytical volleyball.

654
00:37:53,937 --> 00:37:57,658
Since we have to play
with one sign, one style,

655
00:37:57,784 --> 00:37:59,993
and one idea,

656
00:38:00,103 --> 00:38:02,629
I'm preparing a meeting...

657
00:38:03,029 --> 00:38:06,815
so that everyone can understand
and play with the same mindset.

658
00:38:07,389 --> 00:38:09,503
We'll have a look
at their attack patterns.

659
00:38:10,191 --> 00:38:13,291
Most of their attacks come
from the left side.

660
00:38:13,744 --> 00:38:15,943
The ball often comes to position four.

661
00:38:16,177 --> 00:38:18,337
It's called attack distribution.
Do you know what that is?

662
00:38:18,444 --> 00:38:19,898
- No.
- It means the spots...

663
00:38:19,899 --> 00:38:21,749
where they hit the ball most frequently.

664
00:38:22,416 --> 00:38:25,115
They hit most from this area,

665
00:38:25,554 --> 00:38:28,588
so our blockers need
to position themselves right here.

666
00:38:29,523 --> 00:38:34,928
(Blocking: To send the ball back to
the other side by jumping and blocking it)

667
00:38:35,121 --> 00:38:38,465
There's one more reason
I'm telling you to stay at the end here.

668
00:38:39,220 --> 00:38:40,220
Come up.

669
00:38:42,073 --> 00:38:45,186
Let's say you're blocking there,
and I'm a spiker.

670
00:38:45,620 --> 00:38:47,636
I'm about to hit the ball cross-court,

671
00:38:47,796 --> 00:38:49,710
so you positioned yourself here
in advance.

672
00:38:50,029 --> 00:38:52,679
You're positioned here,
and you can play a trick here.

673
00:38:52,680 --> 00:38:54,868
You can play a trick here,

674
00:38:54,874 --> 00:38:56,344
as if you're trying
to block along the line.

675
00:38:57,447 --> 00:38:59,353
And the spiker will think,

676
00:38:59,921 --> 00:39:01,522
"She's blocking along the line."

677
00:39:01,921 --> 00:39:04,425
But you will actually block...

678
00:39:04,859 --> 00:39:05,986
to the side.

679
00:39:07,046 --> 00:39:09,663
Our goal is to make sure...

680
00:39:09,664 --> 00:39:12,332
they don't figure out our tricks
until the end of the game.

681
00:39:12,839 --> 00:39:16,785
I think my extensive overseas experience
as a player...

682
00:39:17,184 --> 00:39:22,509
really helps me when coaching the team.

683
00:39:22,537 --> 00:39:24,550
I prefer efficient...

684
00:39:24,850 --> 00:39:27,814
and meaningful plays.

685
00:39:28,410 --> 00:39:29,924
You need to understand the whole plan...

686
00:39:30,149 --> 00:39:33,253
in order to grasp and execute
the style of volleyball we want to play.

687
00:39:33,487 --> 00:39:36,323
I'm having an enormous number of meetings,

688
00:39:36,630 --> 00:39:39,262
and through them, we continually discuss
not only our plays...

689
00:39:39,769 --> 00:39:43,695
but also programs for the players.

690
00:39:43,944 --> 00:39:48,388
We're already prepared
on how to receive and hit the ball.

691
00:39:49,301 --> 00:39:53,473
I'm sure
the staff members are already very tired.

692
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:59,412
I think they'll say it's really tough
in their individual interview.

693
00:40:00,786 --> 00:40:02,382
It's way too tough.

694
00:40:02,385 --> 00:40:04,251
(Yes, it's way too tough.)

695
00:40:04,264 --> 00:40:05,452
It's really hard.

696
00:40:06,706 --> 00:40:08,322
Did you say, "Stress?"

697
00:40:08,323 --> 00:40:10,561
(They meant it
from the bottom of their hearts.)

698
00:40:10,562 --> 00:40:12,026
I think so.

699
00:40:13,260 --> 00:40:14,228
(Looking away)

700
00:40:14,697 --> 00:40:16,664
It's not defense.

701
00:40:16,665 --> 00:40:20,381
(Regarding the system, even the coaches
can't get away with anything with her.)

702
00:40:20,382 --> 00:40:21,382
Watch.

703
00:40:22,416 --> 00:40:25,528
(The roaring for advanced volleyball)

704
00:40:25,935 --> 00:40:27,428
Who in the world hits it like that?

705
00:40:28,275 --> 00:40:30,377
(She's like a leopard in Kilimanjaro)

706
00:40:30,594 --> 00:40:33,914
I told my coaching staff
to ask me questions anytime...

707
00:40:34,014 --> 00:40:35,633
and that they should understand things...

708
00:40:35,634 --> 00:40:38,018
in order to help the players do the same.

709
00:40:38,406 --> 00:40:39,906
That's what I've been telling them.

710
00:40:40,787 --> 00:40:43,823
(You know what I'm saying, right?)

711
00:40:43,857 --> 00:40:46,393
(Wonder Dogs' Training Schedule,
Afternoon: ball drills)

712
00:40:46,538 --> 00:40:48,350
When you do it, think a little more.

713
00:40:48,691 --> 00:40:50,497
You have to feel every move
while you play.

714
00:40:50,724 --> 00:40:54,450
Just swinging without thinking won't
make you better.

715
00:40:54,890 --> 00:40:57,589
- Understand?
- Yes.

716
00:40:57,637 --> 00:41:00,107
Keep paying attention...

717
00:41:00,356 --> 00:41:01,942
to every fingertip...

718
00:41:02,136 --> 00:41:04,228
- and every toe.
- Okay.

719
00:41:05,248 --> 00:41:07,651
We're going to start blocking drills now.
Everyone, come inside.

720
00:41:12,452 --> 00:41:14,080
I told you to stay near the line!

721
00:41:15,434 --> 00:41:17,891
Come! Come this way now!

722
00:41:19,513 --> 00:41:23,297
(Enkhsoyol left the position
she was supposed to hold.)

723
00:41:23,839 --> 00:41:25,559
I told you to stay here
during rallies too.

724
00:41:25,632 --> 00:41:27,871
- Come here and start from here.
- Okay.

725
00:41:28,311 --> 00:41:31,738
- Play as you think. Stay near the line.
- Okay.

726
00:41:31,894 --> 00:41:33,273
That's where you'll start.

727
00:41:34,094 --> 00:41:35,308
Keep thinking.

728
00:41:35,687 --> 00:41:37,346
The harder it gets,
the more you need to think.

729
00:41:37,760 --> 00:41:39,767
Many of my training methods are...

730
00:41:40,053 --> 00:41:42,525
designed to make it obvious...

731
00:41:42,772 --> 00:41:45,752
when a player isn't thinking
while playing.

732
00:41:46,239 --> 00:41:47,905
I believe...

733
00:41:48,411 --> 00:41:51,658
that you have to play thoughtfully
to keep improving.

734
00:41:51,974 --> 00:41:53,454
"See what's happening right now."

735
00:41:53,674 --> 00:41:55,829
"Hit the ball this way."

736
00:41:55,830 --> 00:41:58,865
I keep telling the players such things
to make them think continuously.

737
00:41:59,933 --> 00:42:01,637
(Enkhsoyol didn't block the ball.)

738
00:42:01,657 --> 00:42:03,370
Again.

739
00:42:03,664 --> 00:42:04,664
Why didn't you jump to block it?

740
00:42:04,907 --> 00:42:06,300
- Enkhsoyol, you should block this side.
- Okay.

741
00:42:07,441 --> 00:42:10,577
(Sol didn't block the ball.)

742
00:42:11,513 --> 00:42:14,699
- Why didn't you jump?
- She was too close.

743
00:42:16,652 --> 00:42:18,836
If you keep doing things your way,

744
00:42:20,965 --> 00:42:22,131
do it somewhere else.

745
00:42:22,445 --> 00:42:25,092
I'm telling you what to do, right?

746
00:42:25,365 --> 00:42:28,375
- How did I say to start playing here?
- From the side.

747
00:42:28,376 --> 00:42:29,717
So, why are you doing it on your own?

748
00:42:31,083 --> 00:42:34,067
We've been doing this so many times.
Don't you get it yet?

749
00:42:34,543 --> 00:42:37,276
We've been at this for an hour,
and you still don't get it? Sol!

750
00:42:37,277 --> 00:42:37,869
I'm sorry!

751
00:42:37,870 --> 00:42:40,215
High plan shoulder taps!

752
00:42:40,804 --> 00:42:44,311
This is a complete mess!

753
00:42:45,392 --> 00:42:47,467
There were too many mistakes happening,

754
00:42:47,603 --> 00:42:49,925
including ones
that shouldn't have happened,

755
00:42:49,926 --> 00:42:51,746
and they kept leading to more errors.

756
00:42:51,865 --> 00:42:54,316
I felt the players needed a push...

757
00:42:54,404 --> 00:42:59,860
to recognize
the seriousness of their mistakes,

758
00:43:00,260 --> 00:43:01,641
so I decided...

759
00:43:01,666 --> 00:43:03,888
to have a Sang Hwa session.

760
00:43:04,376 --> 00:43:05,388
(When the Coach blows the whistle,)

761
00:43:05,389 --> 00:43:06,814
It's a Sang Hwa session.

762
00:43:06,815 --> 00:43:08,786
Guys, get down on your knees for push-ups.

763
00:43:08,787 --> 00:43:10,418
(Sang Hwa is already here.)

764
00:43:11,218 --> 00:43:12,218
Sang Hwa session.

765
00:43:12,691 --> 00:43:14,874
Get ready for the plank.

766
00:43:14,875 --> 00:43:16,869
(For mental prep
and quick-strength training)

767
00:43:16,870 --> 00:43:18,330
Get ready for 20 jumping jacks!

768
00:43:18,844 --> 00:43:21,070
When I played under a foreign coach,

769
00:43:21,443 --> 00:43:23,317
we did similar things.

770
00:43:23,496 --> 00:43:27,120
Players need these kinds of sessions...

771
00:43:27,288 --> 00:43:29,022
to realize
that they've made big mistakes...

772
00:43:29,322 --> 00:43:31,825
and they should work hard to fix them.

773
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:35,128
Are you still doing it the old way today?

774
00:43:35,399 --> 00:43:38,105
Your performance
in the last rally was a disaster!

775
00:43:38,420 --> 00:43:40,100
(Coach Kim's new style is here!)

776
00:43:41,440 --> 00:43:42,919
Think while you play!

777
00:43:43,159 --> 00:43:44,559
Use your brain!

778
00:43:44,578 --> 00:43:45,631
Take it in!

779
00:43:45,632 --> 00:43:46,407
You got it?

780
00:43:46,408 --> 00:43:47,759
(She's emphasized structured play
countless times.)

781
00:43:48,208 --> 00:43:51,478
(Adapting to the new system)

782
00:43:52,771 --> 00:43:54,214
- Hit it!
- Sorry.

783
00:43:54,628 --> 00:43:57,784
Stop apologizing and do it properly first!

784
00:43:59,247 --> 00:44:02,389
How was it? Tell me how it was!

785
00:44:02,760 --> 00:44:04,520
Keep blocking like this.

786
00:44:07,661 --> 00:44:09,930
(Passion at its max)

787
00:44:12,528 --> 00:44:15,068
So many coaches drink often...

788
00:44:15,402 --> 00:44:16,603
and smoke a lot, right?

789
00:44:16,928 --> 00:44:18,687
I kind of understand them,

790
00:44:18,827 --> 00:44:20,139
although I've only had a tiny glimpse yet.

791
00:44:20,540 --> 00:44:23,643
(Gym)

792
00:44:23,644 --> 00:44:26,746
(Clinic)

793
00:44:26,746 --> 00:44:28,848
(Dormitory)

794
00:44:29,349 --> 00:44:30,622
(And...)

795
00:44:30,635 --> 00:44:32,432
(their teamwork is
gradually coming together.)

796
00:44:33,204 --> 00:44:34,335
Nice.

797
00:44:35,922 --> 00:44:37,851
(Wait right there, Geunyoung Girls' High.)

798
00:44:37,891 --> 00:44:38,892
That's it!

799
00:44:38,893 --> 00:44:40,560
(The short yet intense training is over.)

800
00:44:45,098 --> 00:44:49,035
(The day of their fateful first match)

801
00:44:50,971 --> 00:44:55,742
(The die has been cast.)

802
00:44:57,438 --> 00:44:58,438
What?

803
00:44:58,684 --> 00:44:59,880
Oh, my!

804
00:45:00,429 --> 00:45:01,429
What's that?

805
00:45:01,430 --> 00:45:02,789
- What is that?
- Is it...

806
00:45:11,510 --> 00:45:13,043
(Coach Kim's special request)

807
00:45:13,044 --> 00:45:15,003
We would also need a vehicle
for transportation.

808
00:45:21,439 --> 00:45:24,806
(The Victorious Wonder Dogs' team bus)

809
00:45:26,273 --> 00:45:27,673
I can't believe this.

810
00:45:27,673 --> 00:45:29,906
Why did they put the word
"New Head Coach?"

811
00:45:29,939 --> 00:45:31,939
(Kim Yeon Koung, the new head coach)

812
00:45:31,939 --> 00:45:33,906
Why is there my name on it?

813
00:45:34,039 --> 00:45:35,139
Come on.

814
00:45:36,473 --> 00:45:37,606
What is this?

815
00:45:38,573 --> 00:45:40,106
(Rubbing)

816
00:45:40,139 --> 00:45:41,506
Could you look over here?

817
00:45:41,806 --> 00:45:44,239
(Acting modest)

818
00:45:44,373 --> 00:45:46,206
- This looks great.
- Yeah.

819
00:45:46,206 --> 00:45:48,039
We just need to do well in volleyball.

820
00:45:50,119 --> 00:45:51,664
- What do you think, Hey In?
- I'll do my best.

821
00:45:51,665 --> 00:45:53,106
(All for the victory!)

822
00:45:53,106 --> 00:45:54,839
We have everything.
All that's left is the game.

823
00:45:56,388 --> 00:45:59,988
(Jeonju Gymnasium)

824
00:46:00,873 --> 00:46:03,373
(Wonder Dogs' locker room)

825
00:46:10,573 --> 00:46:12,006
I'm getting goosebumps.

826
00:46:12,006 --> 00:46:13,273
It is mind-blowing.

827
00:46:15,739 --> 00:46:16,839
Awesome!

828
00:46:18,606 --> 00:46:19,939
- I'm number 2.
- So amazing.

829
00:46:20,406 --> 00:46:22,773
I'm suddenly getting chills.

830
00:46:22,773 --> 00:46:25,073
But it's cool to see the room
designed like this.

831
00:46:25,073 --> 00:46:26,539
(The Victorious Wonder Dogs' locker room)

832
00:46:26,839 --> 00:46:28,939
- Look at this!
- I like it!

833
00:46:29,639 --> 00:46:33,106
(Written by Manager Boo)

834
00:46:33,106 --> 00:46:34,839
You've got this!

835
00:46:36,406 --> 00:46:39,739
(Manager Boo even showed up
during training a few days ago.)

836
00:46:39,739 --> 00:46:40,739
Nice!

837
00:46:41,267 --> 00:46:43,711
(Running...)

838
00:46:43,712 --> 00:46:45,773
(and running all the time)

839
00:46:46,775 --> 00:46:49,508
(He's here helping
with whatever they need.)

840
00:46:50,912 --> 00:46:54,779
(Trying his best
as the team's new manager)

841
00:46:55,582 --> 00:46:58,382
(Exhausted)

842
00:47:00,806 --> 00:47:03,806
(He shows up first again today.)

843
00:47:04,306 --> 00:47:08,039
(Starting from arranging uniforms,)

844
00:47:09,806 --> 00:47:13,539
(he finishes setting up snacks,
along with red ginseng gifts.)

845
00:47:15,173 --> 00:47:16,606
They must start strong with this.

846
00:47:18,773 --> 00:47:19,939
Please help us win.

847
00:47:21,006 --> 00:47:22,173
We even came to Jeonju.

848
00:47:23,006 --> 00:47:25,773
Coach Kim will be so mad if we lose.

849
00:47:27,139 --> 00:47:29,906
(We must win.)

850
00:47:31,106 --> 00:47:35,539
(The big match is near.)

851
00:47:41,990 --> 00:47:43,790
(Approaching)

852
00:47:48,159 --> 00:47:49,190
I'm here.

853
00:47:50,690 --> 00:47:52,256
(Chuckling)

854
00:47:54,490 --> 00:47:56,090
I love your uniforms!

855
00:47:56,090 --> 00:47:57,390
So is the locker room.

856
00:47:58,090 --> 00:47:59,723
Today,

857
00:48:00,623 --> 00:48:02,690
I'll announce the starting lineup.

858
00:48:03,090 --> 00:48:05,523
For the outside hitters,

859
00:48:06,990 --> 00:48:10,756
it will be Enkhsoyol and Baek Chae Rim.

860
00:48:10,756 --> 00:48:12,290
You two will be outside hitters.

861
00:48:12,790 --> 00:48:14,356
For the middle blocker,

862
00:48:15,890 --> 00:48:20,390
Kim Na Hee and Moon Myoung-Hwa will go.

863
00:48:20,390 --> 00:48:24,323
And Yoon Young In is the opposite hitter.

864
00:48:25,056 --> 00:48:26,823
- Koo Hye In is the libero.
- Okay.

865
00:48:27,756 --> 00:48:28,990
Next.

866
00:48:28,990 --> 00:48:30,856
(The setter of the lineup is...)

867
00:48:31,090 --> 00:48:33,390
Lee Na Yeon is the setter.

868
00:48:33,556 --> 00:48:34,923
You're in the starting lineup.

869
00:48:35,623 --> 00:48:37,490
"Why am I chosen?"

870
00:48:37,890 --> 00:48:40,556
I was half excited and half nervous.

871
00:48:40,990 --> 00:48:44,390
"I may be anxious, but let's focus
on my excitement."

872
00:48:44,456 --> 00:48:48,223
That's what I had in mind
in order to control myself.

873
00:48:50,834 --> 00:48:54,634
(Underdogs' first flight)

874
00:48:55,456 --> 00:49:00,490
(And Kim Yeon Koung's first step
as a head coach)

875
00:49:00,856 --> 00:49:02,790
(To communicate
with performance analysts,)

876
00:49:02,823 --> 00:49:05,690
(she has a walkie-talkie on.)

877
00:49:05,990 --> 00:49:08,490
(The solid Team Yeon Koung enters.)

878
00:49:08,523 --> 00:49:11,223
(Manager Boo is also ready.)

879
00:49:11,290 --> 00:49:14,123
I'm with Lee Suk Ja for today's match
with Geunyoung Girls' High School.

880
00:49:14,123 --> 00:49:15,423
- Hello.
- Hello.

881
00:49:15,723 --> 00:49:17,977
Kim Yeon Koung will debut
as a head coach today.

882
00:49:17,978 --> 00:49:20,478
- That feels different from an athlete.
- It's way different.

883
00:49:20,478 --> 00:49:24,144
"Can my athletes follow my plan properly?"

884
00:49:24,411 --> 00:49:26,578
It's the head coach's role
to make that happen.

885
00:49:26,878 --> 00:49:28,511
So it won't be an easy job.

886
00:49:28,744 --> 00:49:31,178
Players of the Victorious Wonder Dogs...

887
00:49:31,211 --> 00:49:33,078
have their own backgrounds.

888
00:49:33,078 --> 00:49:35,444
Some went through pains,

889
00:49:35,678 --> 00:49:38,211
and others are rebuilding their dream
to be in a pro league.

890
00:49:38,378 --> 00:49:43,178
But that doesn't mean The Wonder Dogs have
endless opportunities.

891
00:49:43,178 --> 00:49:44,744
That's right. We have rules.

892
00:49:45,078 --> 00:49:49,044
Out of seven games, they must win four
to maintain their team.

893
00:49:49,344 --> 00:49:51,678
What happens if they don't win four games?

894
00:49:52,078 --> 00:49:53,211
They'll be disbanded.

895
00:49:54,011 --> 00:49:55,344
Then what about us?

896
00:49:55,544 --> 00:49:57,811
So Wonder Dogs must perform
well in this match.

897
00:49:57,811 --> 00:49:58,911
Of course they should.

898
00:49:59,378 --> 00:50:01,211
By the way, today is their first match.

899
00:50:01,278 --> 00:50:03,144
Their first opposing team is...

900
00:50:03,378 --> 00:50:04,811
Geunyoung Girls' High.

901
00:50:04,811 --> 00:50:08,578
They are energetic and are
full of a fearless spirit.

902
00:50:08,611 --> 00:50:09,611
Here they come.

903
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:24,844
- They are here.
- Hello.

904
00:50:24,844 --> 00:50:28,611
- Hello.
- Hello.

905
00:50:29,411 --> 00:50:31,078
Go strong, Geunyoung!

906
00:50:31,078 --> 00:50:32,178
- Let's go!
- Yeah!

907
00:50:32,178 --> 00:50:36,144
(Their fighting spirit ignites.)

908
00:50:38,244 --> 00:50:41,678
They won the National Middle
and High School Volleyball Championship.

909
00:50:42,611 --> 00:50:46,663
They're one of the top teams,
also consisting of players under 18.

910
00:50:47,278 --> 00:50:50,678
- Jung Sol Min is their libero.
- She's the captain.

911
00:50:51,844 --> 00:50:57,544
(Selected as the first among liberos
in the 2025 draft pick)

912
00:51:02,011 --> 00:51:05,678
(Jin Soo Min, the outside hitter)

913
00:51:07,611 --> 00:51:11,244
Number 14 is short
but has a solid technique.

914
00:51:13,578 --> 00:51:16,578
Unfortunately, in the first match,

915
00:51:16,578 --> 00:51:19,878
Pyo Seung Ju, the ace
of Wonder Dogs, is injured.

916
00:51:19,878 --> 00:51:23,378
She won't be playing today's game
as she needs some time to recover.

917
00:51:24,411 --> 00:51:25,411
Wait, Coach.

918
00:51:26,178 --> 00:51:30,611
(Seung Ju gets injured
accidentally during training.)

919
00:51:30,911 --> 00:51:32,478
I have a bad feeling.

920
00:51:33,044 --> 00:51:35,844
It's a tear even if it's minor.

921
00:51:36,478 --> 00:51:37,944
(She stops training in an emergency.)

922
00:51:37,944 --> 00:51:40,078
I was really enjoying the game.

923
00:51:40,544 --> 00:51:45,844
The ball came fast, and I believed
I could also make it.

924
00:51:47,844 --> 00:51:50,844
"I knew it. I shouldn't have
enjoyed volleyball."

925
00:51:51,278 --> 00:51:52,611
That's what I thought a lot.

926
00:51:53,111 --> 00:51:56,444
I was sorry for the team
that I couldn't help them from the start.

927
00:51:57,078 --> 00:51:58,444
As if I was bothering them.

928
00:51:58,444 --> 00:52:00,944
Geunyoung Girls' High is
Coach Kim's first opponent.

929
00:52:00,944 --> 00:52:03,478
Yet, they are not a team
to be underestimated.

930
00:52:05,611 --> 00:52:06,611
I'm sorry!

931
00:52:08,889 --> 00:52:09,935
My bad.

932
00:52:09,936 --> 00:52:12,772
(Back and forth)

933
00:52:12,773 --> 00:52:13,874
Oh, I'm so sorry!

934
00:52:14,344 --> 00:52:17,711
(The warmup is as fierce
as the actual game.)

935
00:52:19,278 --> 00:52:21,511
Yang Cheol Ho is the head coach
of Geunyoung Girls' High.

936
00:52:21,744 --> 00:52:24,944
He has experience of winning the V-League.

937
00:52:24,944 --> 00:52:26,044
That's right.

938
00:52:26,044 --> 00:52:30,711
No player may outperform
Kim Yeon Koung in our country.

939
00:52:30,978 --> 00:52:35,078
But in terms of coaching,
he's much more superior than she.

940
00:52:35,844 --> 00:52:40,811
Coach Choi Woo Young has led
Geunyoung High School for a long time.

941
00:52:40,811 --> 00:52:44,611
The two elite coaches
elevated their team to the top...

942
00:52:44,644 --> 00:52:47,911
will compete with Kim Yeon Koung,
whose career in coaching has just started.

943
00:52:48,611 --> 00:52:50,511
For the debut match of a new head coach,

944
00:52:50,578 --> 00:52:53,311
she has to go
against two experienced coaches.

945
00:52:54,710 --> 00:52:55,710
Mr. Yang is here.

946
00:52:57,343 --> 00:52:58,343
Hello.

947
00:52:59,043 --> 00:53:01,177
- Coach Kim.
- You lost so much weight.

948
00:53:02,043 --> 00:53:04,543
- Your girls are so good, by the way.
- What do you mean?

949
00:53:04,710 --> 00:53:07,910
Numbers 7 and 14 play well.

950
00:53:08,710 --> 00:53:10,943
They struggled in receiving, though.

951
00:53:11,710 --> 00:53:14,677
The middle blocker is the one
often receiving the ball.

952
00:53:14,677 --> 00:53:15,743
How do you know that?

953
00:53:15,743 --> 00:53:17,877
I watched them, of course.

954
00:53:17,877 --> 00:53:20,263
I can't come here unprepared.

955
00:53:20,510 --> 00:53:22,910
- We can't lose.
- Of course.

956
00:53:23,210 --> 00:53:25,524
Everyone wants to win the match.

957
00:53:27,543 --> 00:53:28,543
Sir.

958
00:53:49,073 --> 00:53:51,206
- I'll be leaving, sir.
- Sure. See you later.

959
00:53:51,719 --> 00:53:52,773
Good luck.

960
00:53:57,473 --> 00:54:00,573
Coach Kim is entering the court.

961
00:54:01,206 --> 00:54:05,706
In Geunyoung Girls' High,
many are set to go to a pro league.

962
00:54:05,838 --> 00:54:09,538
They may be ambitious
to show what they have.

963
00:54:09,633 --> 00:54:11,960
On the other hand,
some of the Wonder Dogs players...

964
00:54:11,961 --> 00:54:16,128
have experienced
the harsh reality of the pro league.

965
00:54:16,128 --> 00:54:18,662
They must be very nervous deep down.

966
00:54:18,662 --> 00:54:19,628
(They have suffered losses.)

967
00:54:19,862 --> 00:54:22,395
If we don't play well,
we're going to get shut down.

968
00:54:22,395 --> 00:54:23,828
I have nothing to lose.

969
00:54:34,028 --> 00:54:36,662
The first game of Coach Yeon Koung...

970
00:54:36,662 --> 00:54:38,462
is about to unfold.

971
00:54:39,195 --> 00:54:42,228
Let's take a look
at the Wonder Dogs' lineup first.

972
00:54:42,228 --> 00:54:43,862
Outside hitter, Enkhsoyol.

973
00:54:43,862 --> 00:54:45,428
Middle blocker, Moon Myoung-Hwa.

974
00:54:45,428 --> 00:54:46,995
Opposite hitter, Yoon Young In.

975
00:54:46,995 --> 00:54:48,562
Outside hitter, Baek Chae Rim.

976
00:54:48,562 --> 00:54:49,928
Middle blocker, Kim Na Hee.

977
00:54:49,928 --> 00:54:51,128
Setter, Lee Na Yeon.

978
00:54:51,128 --> 00:54:52,562
Libero, Koo Hye In.

979
00:54:54,928 --> 00:54:56,862
Their opponent is
Jeonju Geunyoung Girls' High School.

980
00:54:56,862 --> 00:54:58,095
Setter, Ban Ye Bin.

981
00:54:58,095 --> 00:54:59,562
Outside hitter, Jin Soo Min.

982
00:54:59,562 --> 00:55:01,228
Opposite hitter, Oh Eun Chae.

983
00:55:01,228 --> 00:55:02,528
Middle blocker, Yoo Da Eun.

984
00:55:02,528 --> 00:55:04,095
Outside hitter, Kim Yoon Ha.

985
00:55:04,095 --> 00:55:05,495
Middle blocker, Lee Da On.

986
00:55:05,495 --> 00:55:07,428
Libero, Jung Sol Min.

987
00:55:08,562 --> 00:55:10,862
Like I told you,
their play style is short floater serves.

988
00:55:10,862 --> 00:55:13,762
Don't forget the plans
and strategies we went through, okay?

989
00:55:13,762 --> 00:55:15,162
- Yes, coach.
- Yes.

990
00:55:15,162 --> 00:55:17,562
Let's communicate and have fun.

991
00:55:17,562 --> 00:55:19,395
- On three!
- Let's go!

992
00:55:19,395 --> 00:55:22,862
- Let's do this!
- Let's do this!

993
00:55:22,862 --> 00:55:24,962
- Okay!
- We can do this!

994
00:55:24,962 --> 00:55:26,862
- Let's go!
- Let's do this!

995
00:55:27,728 --> 00:55:30,195
Starting with Jeonju
Geunyoung Girls' High School's serve,

996
00:55:30,195 --> 00:55:33,228
we'll kick off the first-ever game
of the Wonder Dogs.

997
00:55:34,862 --> 00:55:36,395
Remember, floating serves.

998
00:55:37,362 --> 00:55:38,928
- Know what I mean, Enkhsoyol?
- Yes, coach.

999
00:55:39,295 --> 00:55:41,462
- Watch out for the short serve.
- Got it.

1000
00:55:41,462 --> 00:55:43,095
Let's go, Wonder Dogs!

1001
00:55:43,095 --> 00:55:45,162
We got this! Let's go!

1002
00:55:45,562 --> 00:55:46,895
Let's do this!

1003
00:55:48,995 --> 00:55:51,095
This is the start of the first set,

1004
00:55:51,095 --> 00:55:53,128
the first ball of play.

1005
00:55:53,128 --> 00:55:56,928
- Players must be very nervous right now.
- Of course, for sure.

1006
00:56:01,162 --> 00:56:05,062
(First serve by Ban Ye Bin)

1007
00:56:07,828 --> 00:56:08,895
Set one is underway.

1008
00:56:10,495 --> 00:56:11,928
She missed the ball.

1009
00:56:16,928 --> 00:56:17,862
Hey!

1010
00:56:25,362 --> 00:56:27,062
What did I say about their serve,
Enkhsoyol?

1011
00:56:27,062 --> 00:56:28,995
- Short.
- And float.

1012
00:56:28,995 --> 00:56:30,128
I told you it'd be a floater.

1013
00:56:30,128 --> 00:56:31,328
You need to move around, not just fast.

1014
00:56:31,328 --> 00:56:32,228
- Got it?
- Yes.

1015
00:56:32,928 --> 00:56:35,195
The serve was perfectly aimed
at Enkhsoyol.

1016
00:56:35,195 --> 00:56:37,462
- It was a target serve.
- Yes.

1017
00:56:37,462 --> 00:56:39,295
Enkhsoyol is strong on offense,

1018
00:56:39,295 --> 00:56:44,062
but like we said earlier,
she needs to work on her passing more.

1019
00:56:44,062 --> 00:56:47,828
And the opposing team hit her
with a target serve.

1020
00:56:48,162 --> 00:56:51,062
First, we need to find the serve rhythm,

1021
00:56:51,062 --> 00:56:52,962
so target Enkhsoyol
when the situation is right.

1022
00:56:52,962 --> 00:56:54,295
(A targeted serve on Enkhsoyol)

1023
00:56:54,295 --> 00:56:55,228
- Got it?
- Yes.

1024
00:56:55,228 --> 00:56:57,295
We need to aim for the weak passes.

1025
00:56:58,062 --> 00:57:01,795
(The veteran coach's tactic is paying
off from the start.)

1026
00:57:02,328 --> 00:57:03,462
I told you it'd be a floater.

1027
00:57:03,462 --> 00:57:04,695
You need to move around, not just fast.

1028
00:57:04,695 --> 00:57:06,128
- Got it?
- Yes.

1029
00:57:06,128 --> 00:57:07,195
- You know what I mean?
- Yes.

1030
00:57:07,195 --> 00:57:08,562
Floating serves.

1031
00:57:09,928 --> 00:57:12,595
(Another serve
from Geunyoung Girls' High School)

1032
00:57:13,362 --> 00:57:14,495
The score is one to zero.

1033
00:57:17,795 --> 00:57:19,328
(Did they make the pass?)

1034
00:57:20,728 --> 00:57:21,962
Lee Da On's setter dump!

1035
00:57:25,195 --> 00:57:26,362
(Scrambling save)

1036
00:57:26,562 --> 00:57:27,395
They saved it.

1037
00:57:27,728 --> 00:57:28,762
A spike!

1038
00:57:30,328 --> 00:57:31,928
(No way!)

1039
00:57:33,795 --> 00:57:34,728
Passed on.

1040
00:57:35,362 --> 00:57:37,228
(Barely keeping it alive)

1041
00:57:39,595 --> 00:57:40,395
Hit it!

1042
00:57:40,828 --> 00:57:42,562
Spike by Jin Soo Min!

1043
00:57:44,128 --> 00:57:46,495
- All right.
- Ball is out.

1044
00:57:46,828 --> 00:57:49,462
(Thank goodness.)

1045
00:57:49,462 --> 00:57:50,662
Sorry, Hye In.

1046
00:57:51,362 --> 00:57:52,995
It's okay. We're okay.

1047
00:57:53,562 --> 00:57:56,095
The Wonder Dogs scored their first point
since their establishment.

1048
00:57:56,095 --> 00:57:56,995
It's a 1 to 1 tie.

1049
00:57:59,195 --> 00:58:01,795
(The first one to serve
for the Wonder Dogs is...)

1050
00:58:02,962 --> 00:58:04,028
Moon Myoung-Hwa's serve.

1051
00:58:10,695 --> 00:58:12,062
Darn it!

1052
00:58:14,595 --> 00:58:16,395
She served into the net.

1053
00:58:16,728 --> 00:58:18,995
(A serving error)

1054
00:58:21,095 --> 00:58:22,162
So close.

1055
00:58:22,162 --> 00:58:23,028
That was not close.

1056
00:58:23,528 --> 00:58:24,628
That was very close.

1057
00:58:26,595 --> 00:58:28,695
Geunyoung Girls' High School leads 2 to 1.

1058
00:58:29,462 --> 00:58:33,862
- Nice serve, Jin Soo Min!
- Nice serve, Jin Soo Min!

1059
00:58:34,895 --> 00:58:35,928
Here she is.

1060
00:58:35,928 --> 00:58:38,128
Geunyoung Girls' High School's ace.
Jin Soo Min.

1061
00:58:40,062 --> 00:58:41,762
Let's focus!

1062
00:58:41,928 --> 00:58:43,562
Just pop it up. I'll take the set.

1063
00:58:43,562 --> 00:58:44,528
Okay.

1064
00:58:44,528 --> 00:58:47,195
Watch out for the floater.

1065
00:58:47,762 --> 00:58:50,262
Move around. Move a lot.

1066
00:58:59,862 --> 00:59:02,128
(Another bad reception)

1067
00:59:02,495 --> 00:59:03,895
Ace by Jin Soo Min!

1068
00:59:04,828 --> 00:59:05,962
I told you to move, Enkhsoyol.

1069
00:59:05,962 --> 00:59:07,028
Why aren't you moving around?

1070
00:59:07,028 --> 00:59:07,862
Okay, coach.

1071
00:59:08,726 --> 00:59:09,795
Her answer is clear, at least.

1072
00:59:12,162 --> 00:59:13,328
It's thee to one now.

1073
00:59:13,795 --> 00:59:16,595
(Another serve by Jin Soo Min)

1074
00:59:20,362 --> 00:59:21,395
(Finally, a successful reception)

1075
00:59:21,395 --> 00:59:22,462
That was a good reception.

1076
00:59:22,462 --> 00:59:23,295
A high ball.
Spike!

1077
00:59:25,328 --> 00:59:26,295
(Blocked)

1078
00:59:29,862 --> 00:59:31,828
(A powerful spike)

1079
00:59:32,428 --> 00:59:34,828
Up it goes, aiming for the middle!

1080
00:59:34,828 --> 00:59:35,895
She missed.

1081
00:59:38,928 --> 00:59:39,795
Okay!

1082
00:59:41,662 --> 00:59:45,462
- Geunyoung Girls' High School leads...
- That was Yoo Da Eun's play.

1083
00:59:45,828 --> 00:59:49,628
The players from Geunyoung
Girls' High School are pretty powerful.

1084
00:59:49,628 --> 00:59:50,895
Their offense is looking strong.

1085
00:59:50,895 --> 00:59:51,828
That's right.

1086
00:59:52,195 --> 00:59:55,462
Compared to Geunyoung Girls' High School,

1087
00:59:55,462 --> 00:59:57,628
Wonder Dogs players are quite tense.

1088
00:59:57,628 --> 00:59:59,695
They seem a bit stiff.

1089
01:00:00,395 --> 01:00:02,162
(Three serves in a row)

1090
01:00:02,462 --> 01:00:04,695
(Jin Soo Min)

1091
01:00:05,662 --> 01:00:09,595
- Nice serve, Jin Soo Min.
- Nice serve, Jin Soo Min.

1092
01:00:12,895 --> 01:00:14,595
(Nice receive)

1093
01:00:14,595 --> 01:00:16,095
Yes, carry on!

1094
01:00:16,095 --> 01:00:16,995
To the left,

1095
01:00:16,995 --> 01:00:18,062
and she sent it over!

1096
01:00:19,428 --> 01:00:20,428
(Easy)

1097
01:00:20,428 --> 01:00:21,828
Ban Ye Bin is back on defense.

1098
01:00:21,828 --> 01:00:22,795
The ball is tossed.

1099
01:00:23,495 --> 01:00:25,295
(Kim Yoon Ha's spike)

1100
01:00:25,828 --> 01:00:27,328
Open spike!

1101
01:00:28,462 --> 01:00:29,695
Sorry.

1102
01:00:29,695 --> 01:00:30,695
Let's carry on.

1103
01:00:31,828 --> 01:00:33,628
That's a point!

1104
01:00:35,328 --> 01:00:39,362
Geunyoung Girls' High School is off
to a fierce start.

1105
01:00:39,362 --> 01:00:40,295
It's five to one.

1106
01:00:44,062 --> 01:00:46,762
We're in big trouble.

1107
01:00:46,762 --> 01:00:47,728
What do we do?

1108
01:00:47,728 --> 01:00:49,695
I felt like we were lost on the court.

1109
01:00:49,962 --> 01:00:52,995
We needed to find our rhythm again,

1110
01:00:53,628 --> 01:00:55,328
but I couldn't figure out how to do it.

1111
01:00:55,328 --> 01:00:57,362
Which direction should we go?

1112
01:00:57,362 --> 01:01:00,762
Things got a bit complicated in my mind.

1113
01:01:04,895 --> 01:01:06,995
Jin Soo Min on a serving run.

1114
01:01:06,995 --> 01:01:08,762
This is already her fourth serve.

1115
01:01:12,462 --> 01:01:14,595
This time,
she couldn't get it over the net.

1116
01:01:15,128 --> 01:01:17,495
(The bleeding finally stops.)

1117
01:01:17,928 --> 01:01:19,162
Let's stay calm.

1118
01:01:19,162 --> 01:01:20,528
Don't let your guard down.

1119
01:01:20,528 --> 01:01:21,862
Nice serve!

1120
01:01:23,095 --> 01:01:25,162
(A golden chance to close the gap)

1121
01:01:25,795 --> 01:01:27,728
(Yoon Young In's serve)

1122
01:01:28,762 --> 01:01:30,062
(Solid defense)

1123
01:01:30,062 --> 01:01:30,928
Nice pass.

1124
01:01:30,928 --> 01:01:32,528
Spike on the received ball!

1125
01:01:33,662 --> 01:01:34,828
They saved it.

1126
01:01:34,828 --> 01:01:35,728
(Unstable sequence)

1127
01:01:36,462 --> 01:01:37,395
They sent it back over.

1128
01:01:37,395 --> 01:01:38,428
It's in the opponent's court.

1129
01:01:38,862 --> 01:01:39,795
They passed the ball,

1130
01:01:39,795 --> 01:01:41,228
and Yoo Da Eun spikes!

1131
01:01:41,228 --> 01:01:42,262
Wait, timeout!

1132
01:01:42,762 --> 01:01:45,862
(Was that off the block and out?)

1133
01:01:46,428 --> 01:01:49,795
(If it touched the arm,
it's a point lost for the Wonder Dogs.)

1134
01:01:50,128 --> 01:01:51,428
No, timeout!

1135
01:01:51,428 --> 01:01:53,862
- She touched it!
- That was a block touch!

1136
01:01:54,328 --> 01:01:55,495
(The officials say...)

1137
01:01:55,495 --> 01:01:57,462
(no touch on that play.)

1138
01:01:57,562 --> 01:01:58,528
Great job!

1139
01:01:58,528 --> 01:02:00,095
(Thank goodness)

1140
01:02:00,528 --> 01:02:02,362
- All right.
- Nice play.

1141
01:02:02,362 --> 01:02:04,862
They called it a no-touch.

1142
01:02:04,862 --> 01:02:06,662
- Wasn't it a touch?
- Check the replay!

1143
01:02:06,662 --> 01:02:07,528
It was a touch.

1144
01:02:08,695 --> 01:02:09,962
Let's ask for a challenge.

1145
01:02:09,962 --> 01:02:11,295
- Should we press it?
- Press it.

1146
01:02:12,462 --> 01:02:14,462
A video review request is being made.

1147
01:02:15,295 --> 01:02:17,062
(Would 47 years
of combined experience be right?)

1148
01:02:18,395 --> 01:02:21,562
The ball did come up a bit short.

1149
01:02:23,795 --> 01:02:25,395
(It touched the net, not the arm.)

1150
01:02:25,395 --> 01:02:26,962
Yes, it's clear.

1151
01:02:28,128 --> 01:02:29,662
(Point for Wonder Dogs)

1152
01:02:29,662 --> 01:02:31,995
- Nice!
- Yes!

1153
01:02:31,995 --> 01:02:33,328
Good move!

1154
01:02:33,328 --> 01:02:36,028
It clipped the net and landed out.

1155
01:02:36,795 --> 01:02:38,062
It's five to three now.

1156
01:02:41,062 --> 01:02:43,795
- Let's not be hasty.
- Stay calm.

1157
01:02:43,795 --> 01:02:45,462
We can't keep going like this.

1158
01:02:46,062 --> 01:02:48,562
We need something more powerful.

1159
01:02:49,395 --> 01:02:50,228
Na Yeon.

1160
01:02:50,528 --> 01:02:53,395
Their hitters are moving
better than we expected,

1161
01:02:53,395 --> 01:02:54,962
- so go with a long set.
- Yes, coach.

1162
01:02:54,962 --> 01:02:57,162
- Let's raise the tempo.
- Got it.

1163
01:02:57,162 --> 01:02:59,828
Coach Yeon Koung pulled Na Yeon aside...

1164
01:02:59,828 --> 01:03:02,362
and told her to go with longer sets.

1165
01:03:03,228 --> 01:03:05,662
(Yoon Young In's serve)

1166
01:03:10,462 --> 01:03:11,728
A fast pass to the left.

1167
01:03:14,428 --> 01:03:15,628
They tossed it up.

1168
01:03:15,628 --> 01:03:19,595
Running up front for an attack!

1169
01:03:19,595 --> 01:03:22,162
- Yes, that's the way to go!
- That was a nice play.

1170
01:03:24,262 --> 01:03:27,028
(First attack point in the team's history)

1171
01:03:27,228 --> 01:03:28,895
The score is now five to four.

1172
01:03:30,095 --> 01:03:31,928
(Way to go!)

1173
01:03:33,728 --> 01:03:36,462
(Just like Coach Yeon Koung ordered...)

1174
01:03:37,862 --> 01:03:40,728
Coach Yeon Koung's new tactic worked.

1175
01:03:41,128 --> 01:03:43,928
(The opponents got lost
in the longer set.)

1176
01:03:44,528 --> 01:03:48,262
That's Kim Na Hee's signature play.

1177
01:03:48,262 --> 01:03:51,128
She's great
with quick attacks off her speed.

1178
01:03:51,695 --> 01:03:54,828
Her footwork is
as fast as Brazil's soccer players.

1179
01:03:55,128 --> 01:03:57,362
(With Wonder Dogs' fast steps,)

1180
01:03:58,762 --> 01:03:59,995
(the opposing team is shaken.)

1181
01:03:59,995 --> 01:04:01,262
Let's do this!

1182
01:04:01,528 --> 01:04:04,128
(Let's close the gap!)

1183
01:04:04,128 --> 01:04:05,195
Nice.

1184
01:04:05,195 --> 01:04:06,395
Nice play, guys.

1185
01:04:08,228 --> 01:04:09,062
Listen.

1186
01:04:09,355 --> 01:04:14,295
If you attack from the side,
Na Hee will block the inside.

1187
01:04:21,362 --> 01:04:23,962
(First set, Geunyoung Girls' High 6
: Wonder Dogs 4)

1188
01:04:25,228 --> 01:04:27,628
Here's Eun Chae
from Geunyoung Girls' High serving.

1189
01:04:30,362 --> 01:04:31,328
That's a good serve.

1190
01:04:31,328 --> 01:04:33,328
Back A!

1191
01:04:34,228 --> 01:04:36,462
(A similar opportunity...)

1192
01:04:37,328 --> 01:04:40,028
(to the previous scoring situation)

1193
01:04:43,162 --> 01:04:44,095
She moved her position again.

1194
01:04:45,762 --> 01:04:47,128
(Defending it easily)

1195
01:04:47,128 --> 01:04:48,728
They were slightly out of sync.

1196
01:04:51,519 --> 01:04:54,053
Hit it!

1197
01:04:54,462 --> 01:04:55,362
Will it be a quick follow-up?

1198
01:04:57,162 --> 01:04:58,928
She makes a diving dig!

1199
01:05:05,762 --> 01:05:07,728
The defense couldn't hold.

1200
01:05:08,895 --> 01:05:09,728
Hey!

1201
01:05:11,862 --> 01:05:13,562
Yes!

1202
01:05:14,028 --> 01:05:15,995
- Great job!
- You did well!

1203
01:05:15,995 --> 01:05:17,062
(It's easy!)

1204
01:05:17,928 --> 01:05:19,095
Na Yeon.

1205
01:05:19,095 --> 01:05:21,295
Hey, why did you go for a Back A
when she was already up?

1206
01:05:21,295 --> 01:05:22,528
- Watch her position carefully,
- Okay.

1207
01:05:22,528 --> 01:05:23,595
and stop using Back A!

1208
01:05:25,162 --> 01:05:29,062
(Back A: a type of quick attack)

1209
01:05:30,062 --> 01:05:33,295
(Depending on the distance
of the setter's toss,)

1210
01:05:33,843 --> 01:05:38,277
(a 1-meter quick is called an A Quick,)

1211
01:05:38,995 --> 01:05:43,495
(a 2-meter quick is a B Quick,)

1212
01:05:44,195 --> 01:05:48,662
(and anything beyond 3 meters is
a C Quick.)

1213
01:05:49,728 --> 01:05:50,762
(Back tosses are called Back A or Back B.)

1214
01:05:50,762 --> 01:05:53,562
(Back A)

1215
01:05:54,628 --> 01:05:57,762
(Back B)

1216
01:05:58,662 --> 01:06:02,995
(A quick attack is great for its speed,)

1217
01:06:04,462 --> 01:06:08,262
(but if the opponent catches the timing,)

1218
01:06:08,928 --> 01:06:12,328
(it can be blocked easily.)

1219
01:06:12,328 --> 01:06:14,962
If you attack from the side,
Na Hee will block the inside.

1220
01:06:15,228 --> 01:06:17,228
The players
from Geunyoung Girls' High are...

1221
01:06:17,228 --> 01:06:20,928
reading where Setter Na Yeon will set
and defending well.

1222
01:06:20,928 --> 01:06:22,462
The gap was closed to just one point,

1223
01:06:22,462 --> 01:06:24,328
but the lead has stretched
back to three points.

1224
01:06:28,628 --> 01:06:30,662
- That's an impressive serve.
- That was sharp.

1225
01:06:34,662 --> 01:06:36,862
(There's an open space,)

1226
01:06:37,928 --> 01:06:39,995
(but he tossed short.)

1227
01:06:41,895 --> 01:06:44,062
The ball didn't clear the net.

1228
01:06:45,162 --> 01:06:46,462
(Don't you dare!)

1229
01:06:48,728 --> 01:06:50,395
- I'm sorry.
- The score is 8 to 4,

1230
01:06:50,395 --> 01:06:51,995
a four-point difference.

1231
01:06:54,062 --> 01:06:55,128
There it is.

1232
01:06:55,128 --> 01:06:56,062
Okay, good.

1233
01:06:56,062 --> 01:06:57,162
Chae Rim receives it.

1234
01:06:58,095 --> 01:06:58,995
Power hit!

1235
01:06:59,728 --> 01:07:01,095
(But it headed right into the defender.)

1236
01:07:01,095 --> 01:07:02,162
She keeps the ball in the air.

1237
01:07:03,337 --> 01:07:04,537
Spike!

1238
01:07:04,562 --> 01:07:05,762
The block fails!

1239
01:07:05,762 --> 01:07:07,328
(Na Yeon failed to block it.)

1240
01:07:08,628 --> 01:07:12,228
(First set, Geunyoung Girls' High 6
: Wonder Dogs 4)

1241
01:07:13,595 --> 01:07:14,695
Left!

1242
01:07:17,395 --> 01:07:20,095
(Na Yeon failed to block it again.)

1243
01:07:21,195 --> 01:07:22,862
I'm so sorry.

1244
01:07:22,862 --> 01:07:24,056
Back to the position!

1245
01:07:27,662 --> 01:07:28,662
Nice reception.

1246
01:07:29,428 --> 01:07:30,328
(Short toss?)

1247
01:07:31,795 --> 01:07:33,128
(A short one again)

1248
01:07:34,128 --> 01:07:34,995
It's too low.

1249
01:07:35,662 --> 01:07:37,195
(Not a chance)

1250
01:07:37,362 --> 01:07:38,495
The ball lifted the ball.

1251
01:07:41,062 --> 01:07:43,162
What a spike!

1252
01:07:43,162 --> 01:07:44,495
(Consecutive points for the opponent)

1253
01:07:45,128 --> 01:07:47,028
I'm really sorry.

1254
01:07:47,028 --> 01:07:47,928
You can't let that slip!

1255
01:07:47,928 --> 01:07:50,628
Wonder Dogs' offense isn't
really getting going.

1256
01:07:50,628 --> 01:07:54,162
Apart from Na Hee's
right-side attack score,

1257
01:07:54,162 --> 01:07:56,462
they haven't managed any points
from their attacks so far.

1258
01:07:56,462 --> 01:08:00,762
Meanwhile, the Geunyoung High players
are clearly enjoying themselves out there.

1259
01:08:00,762 --> 01:08:03,862
Now, this could rattle Wonder Dogs a bit.

1260
01:08:03,862 --> 01:08:05,228
Yes, they might feel a little pressured.

1261
01:08:07,862 --> 01:08:09,995
I could feel trouble was brewing.

1262
01:08:10,728 --> 01:08:12,595
I thought, "Seriously?"

1263
01:08:13,028 --> 01:08:14,628
We needed to do something,

1264
01:08:15,495 --> 01:08:18,762
or it could become serious trouble.

1265
01:08:20,843 --> 01:08:21,795
Timeout.

1266
01:08:26,228 --> 01:08:27,962
Wonder Dogs called a timeout.

1267
01:08:27,962 --> 01:08:29,062
Na Yeon, come here.

1268
01:08:30,895 --> 01:08:37,128
Why are you going for a back B?

1269
01:08:37,128 --> 01:08:38,595
I told you to give a long set.

1270
01:08:38,595 --> 01:08:42,195
Unless you can do it with precision,
Back B or Back A can't be an option.

1271
01:08:42,195 --> 01:08:43,462
Lift it up with a run,

1272
01:08:43,462 --> 01:08:45,595
and when Young In moves,
give her a long set through the pipe.

1273
01:08:45,595 --> 01:08:47,228
Open it all up,

1274
01:08:47,228 --> 01:08:48,428
so she can stop in the middle comfortably.

1275
01:08:48,428 --> 01:08:49,495
Understand?

1276
01:08:49,495 --> 01:08:52,195
She kept making a short toss to Na Hee,

1277
01:08:52,195 --> 01:08:54,862
so Coach Kim told her to execute
the long play they practiced.

1278
01:08:54,862 --> 01:08:56,895
It means using multiple strategies to keep
the opposing middle blockers...

1279
01:08:56,895 --> 01:08:59,262
- from keeping up.
- That's right.

1280
01:08:59,262 --> 01:09:02,095
The focus was on utilizing Young In a lot.

1281
01:09:03,328 --> 01:09:06,362
They did it completely differently
from what we discussed,

1282
01:09:07,095 --> 01:09:08,895
so I got upset.

1283
01:09:09,395 --> 01:09:14,495
The efficiency of our attackers depends...

1284
01:09:14,495 --> 01:09:19,295
greatly on the setters' choices
and accuracy.

1285
01:09:19,295 --> 01:09:22,128
That's why the setter position is crucial.

1286
01:09:23,128 --> 01:09:24,995
Everything is in a mess.

1287
01:09:25,628 --> 01:09:27,262
I was quite nervous.

1288
01:09:28,228 --> 01:09:30,428
I made a big mistake on the back toss.

1289
01:09:33,295 --> 01:09:35,095
My hands started shaking.

1290
01:09:37,828 --> 01:09:40,595
So, I focus on the mental aspect.

1291
01:09:41,162 --> 01:09:43,295
It's likely to happen again.

1292
01:09:45,962 --> 01:09:47,562
What if I make the same mistake?

1293
01:09:47,562 --> 01:09:48,428
Why did I even mess it up?

1294
01:09:49,662 --> 01:09:53,095
I was beating myself up
over my own mistake.

1295
01:09:54,595 --> 01:09:56,828
I felt like I might make the error again.

1296
01:09:56,828 --> 01:09:58,128
(There was this anxiety
that she could fail again.)

1297
01:09:58,795 --> 01:10:00,166
(Coach Kim reminds them of their plan.)

1298
01:10:00,167 --> 01:10:02,262
- A short one.
- That's right, a short one.

1299
01:10:02,262 --> 01:10:03,162
- Got it?
- Yes.

1300
01:10:03,162 --> 01:10:04,662
How many points did you let through
on the short ones?

1301
01:10:04,662 --> 01:10:05,795
A lot.

1302
01:10:06,262 --> 01:10:08,128
What about the long serve?

1303
01:10:08,528 --> 01:10:10,795
- None.
- You only gave up on the short ones.

1304
01:10:10,795 --> 01:10:12,895
I keep telling you to focus
on the short serves!

1305
01:10:12,895 --> 01:10:14,428
- Take it seriously.
- Okay.

1306
01:10:19,695 --> 01:10:21,528
Focus on reception.

1307
01:10:21,528 --> 01:10:22,495
A good reception is needed...

1308
01:10:22,495 --> 01:10:24,462
- for a good set and a strong hit.
- Okay.

1309
01:10:24,462 --> 01:10:26,262
- Let's get the vibe back.
- Okay.

1310
01:10:26,262 --> 01:10:28,228
And when you're subbed in,
keep shouting and cheering a lot.

1311
01:10:28,228 --> 01:10:30,095
We've been too nervous.

1312
01:10:30,728 --> 01:10:35,795
Hey.

1313
01:10:35,795 --> 01:10:37,262
It's not about the vibe.

1314
01:10:37,262 --> 01:10:39,428
- You need to play proper volleyball.
- Okay.

1315
01:10:39,428 --> 01:10:41,462
I'm talking about proper volleyball.

1316
01:10:41,462 --> 01:10:42,928
- Do the things we've talked about so far.
- Okay.

1317
01:10:42,928 --> 01:10:44,628
What did I tell you about serve reception?

1318
01:10:44,628 --> 01:10:45,528
Short ones.

1319
01:10:45,528 --> 01:10:48,028
- Short ones first.
- That's what I've been telling you.

1320
01:10:48,028 --> 01:10:50,362
What happens if we attack
through the middle?

1321
01:10:50,362 --> 01:10:51,595
- They'll follow us.
- The middle blockers will follow, right?

1322
01:10:51,595 --> 01:10:53,295
Then, why did you go for a quick attack?

1323
01:10:53,295 --> 01:10:55,528
Think about things like this.
It's not about the vibe, you little.

1324
01:10:55,528 --> 01:10:57,462
- Keep thinking.
- Okay.

1325
01:10:58,928 --> 01:11:00,728
- "You little" just came out.
- Yes.

1326
01:11:01,362 --> 01:11:03,162
She gritted her teeth.

1327
01:11:03,595 --> 01:11:05,228
She told them what to do,

1328
01:11:05,228 --> 01:11:07,462
but once the game started,
they were doing something else.

1329
01:11:07,462 --> 01:11:09,328
Because of that,

1330
01:11:09,328 --> 01:11:11,595
she kept talking
until her voice got hoarse.

1331
01:11:12,362 --> 01:11:14,228
As a coach,

1332
01:11:14,228 --> 01:11:16,428
she has to go through that every day.

1333
01:11:17,728 --> 01:11:18,662
Hey.

1334
01:11:19,662 --> 01:11:22,528
Back A and Back B never go through.
Why do you keep trying them?

1335
01:11:23,562 --> 01:11:25,528
Open it up and run...

1336
01:11:25,528 --> 01:11:27,528
It's obvious she's a rookie coach.

1337
01:11:27,528 --> 01:11:30,795
- She's not supposed to be on the court.
- She's on the court.

1338
01:11:30,795 --> 01:11:32,995
She really can't go in there.

1339
01:11:33,428 --> 01:11:35,128
That was a tricky situation!

1340
01:11:35,128 --> 01:11:37,062
(When it's tricky, go for a long toss!)

1341
01:11:37,628 --> 01:11:38,962
Let's go, girls!

1342
01:11:39,462 --> 01:11:40,328
Young In!

1343
01:11:41,162 --> 01:11:42,928
It's all right. Relax!

1344
01:11:44,962 --> 01:11:46,328
My pride was hurt.

1345
01:11:47,195 --> 01:11:49,362
I wanted to prove myself again.

1346
01:11:50,362 --> 01:11:51,795
Forget the score,

1347
01:11:51,795 --> 01:11:55,495
I just decided
to loosen up my stiff body first.

1348
01:11:59,428 --> 01:12:00,562
Myoung-Hwa.

1349
01:12:00,562 --> 01:12:02,395
(Got it.)

1350
01:12:03,795 --> 01:12:05,862
(Yoon Ha's serve)

1351
01:12:08,428 --> 01:12:09,462
Her serve isn't stable.

1352
01:12:11,462 --> 01:12:12,595
Here's Yoon Ha's serve.

1353
01:12:21,095 --> 01:12:22,228
She scores!

1354
01:12:22,228 --> 01:12:23,962
Nice!

1355
01:12:23,962 --> 01:12:24,962
Awesome!

1356
01:12:25,728 --> 01:12:26,995
I'll keep setting it up for you.

1357
01:12:27,895 --> 01:12:29,728
Thank you!

1358
01:12:29,728 --> 01:12:30,895
- Thanks.
- Nice job, Young In.

1359
01:12:30,895 --> 01:12:32,895
- Thank you.
- That was great, Young In.

1360
01:12:32,895 --> 01:12:35,462
- Tell her to feed you more!
- Okay!

1361
01:12:36,495 --> 01:12:38,728
(Exchanging signals)

1362
01:12:39,571 --> 01:12:41,171
(There goes Myoung-Hwa.)

1363
01:12:42,762 --> 01:12:44,195
(Tricking the opposing team,
using Myoung-Hwa)

1364
01:12:44,437 --> 01:12:47,803
Na Yeon gave Young In a nice, long toss.

1365
01:12:47,828 --> 01:12:50,962
They need to keep setting Young In up,

1366
01:12:50,962 --> 01:12:52,628
so she can hit the ball hard for a point.

1367
01:12:52,628 --> 01:12:55,362
Coach Kim must have asked...

1368
01:12:55,362 --> 01:12:57,462
for this kind of play a lot.

1369
01:13:00,462 --> 01:13:02,462
(Stiff)

1370
01:13:11,062 --> 01:13:12,795
Tossing backward.

1371
01:13:14,362 --> 01:13:16,328
(Throwing her body to defense)

1372
01:13:18,128 --> 01:13:19,828
She dove to make the defense.

1373
01:13:23,362 --> 01:13:25,350
- To the left, she lifts the ball again.
- Mine.

1374
01:13:29,595 --> 01:13:31,962
(Which way will the ball go?)

1375
01:13:34,195 --> 01:13:35,662
(Young In's spike)

1376
01:13:35,662 --> 01:13:36,828
Spike!

1377
01:13:36,828 --> 01:13:38,195
The ball is out!

1378
01:13:39,228 --> 01:13:41,162
(Breaking through the block)

1379
01:13:41,162 --> 01:13:42,128
Young In.

1380
01:13:46,228 --> 01:13:49,762
- Young In has real punching power.
- That's right.

1381
01:13:49,762 --> 01:13:51,828
It's a good idea to set it high...

1382
01:13:51,828 --> 01:13:55,262
and let Yoon Young In handle the attack,
just like now.

1383
01:13:56,062 --> 01:13:59,895
Na Yeon, feed it further inside.

1384
01:14:00,895 --> 01:14:03,228
Wonder Dogs are narrowing the score gap.

1385
01:14:03,928 --> 01:14:06,762
(First set, Geunyoung Girls' High 6
: Wonder Dogs 4)

1386
01:14:11,488 --> 01:14:12,788
(Where will the ball go this time?)

1387
01:14:13,288 --> 01:14:14,421
(Nervous)

1388
01:14:18,502 --> 01:14:20,264
(She tosses in a long distance again!)

1389
01:14:21,288 --> 01:14:22,788
(Yoon Young In gains three points.)

1390
01:14:23,621 --> 01:14:25,855
Na-Yeon.

1391
01:14:26,488 --> 01:14:28,188
(Nice!)

1392
01:14:28,755 --> 01:14:30,221
Great job.

1393
01:14:30,221 --> 01:14:31,988
Way to go!

1394
01:14:32,288 --> 01:14:34,255
(Sighing)

1395
01:14:34,988 --> 01:14:37,621
I got excited at that point.

1396
01:14:38,055 --> 01:14:40,288
One of the puzzles was solved.

1397
01:14:40,921 --> 01:14:42,955
I believed that if we followed Coach Kim,

1398
01:14:44,321 --> 01:14:45,521
we might win.

1399
01:14:46,321 --> 01:14:47,588
Let's chat while we play.

1400
01:14:47,588 --> 01:14:50,255
We need to bring some energy in!

1401
01:14:52,902 --> 01:14:53,745
(Focus, everyone!)

1402
01:14:59,055 --> 01:15:00,388
(Jin Soo Min's powerful spike)

1403
01:15:01,321 --> 01:15:03,888
It bounces off from the left.

1404
01:15:04,755 --> 01:15:05,821
It's a chance ball!

1405
01:15:05,821 --> 01:15:07,088
Give it back!

1406
01:15:12,188 --> 01:15:14,155
(A high toss to Young In again!)

1407
01:15:14,988 --> 01:15:17,555
(Yoon Young In scores four points.)

1408
01:15:18,188 --> 01:15:19,588
Let's have fun!

1409
01:15:20,788 --> 01:15:22,255
(Smiling)

1410
01:15:23,921 --> 01:15:25,588
Nice job, Young In.

1411
01:15:27,821 --> 01:15:29,788
(Let's go after them!)

1412
01:15:32,521 --> 01:15:33,921
(Breathing deeply)

1413
01:15:39,588 --> 01:15:40,721
To the back.

1414
01:15:42,560 --> 01:15:43,854
(A fearless block)

1415
01:15:49,288 --> 01:15:52,555
(Yoon Young In's spike)

1416
01:15:52,555 --> 01:15:54,888
(She scores five points.)

1417
01:15:56,155 --> 01:15:58,121
Wonder Dogs continues to score!

1418
01:16:01,521 --> 01:16:03,355
(They are only two points behind.)

1419
01:16:03,988 --> 01:16:05,521
(With Na-Yeon fully warmed up,)

1420
01:16:06,255 --> 01:16:08,555
(Back Chae-Rim scores.)

1421
01:16:13,055 --> 01:16:14,288
Okay!

1422
01:16:14,288 --> 01:16:16,321
(Back Chae-Rim is on a scoring streak.)

1423
01:16:16,321 --> 01:16:18,588
They've finally tied the game.

1424
01:16:18,855 --> 01:16:21,221
Young In,
you focus too much on the inside.

1425
01:16:21,221 --> 01:16:24,555
(Instructing her to spike outside)

1426
01:16:27,807 --> 01:16:29,218
A chance to turn the tables!

1427
01:16:36,655 --> 01:16:38,255
It's heading to the right!

1428
01:16:40,088 --> 01:16:41,688
(An outside spike)

1429
01:16:42,155 --> 01:16:43,388
(Is it out?)

1430
01:16:44,121 --> 01:16:46,521
(Or is it in?)

1431
01:16:48,388 --> 01:16:50,055
(In)

1432
01:16:54,188 --> 01:16:56,421
Wonder Dogs turned the tables!

1433
01:17:01,655 --> 01:17:02,688
It's in?

1434
01:17:03,048 --> 01:17:06,348
With the scores of 17 to 16,
Wonder Dogs takes back the lead.

1435
01:17:06,855 --> 01:17:11,655
The sequence worked perfectly
through all three steps.

1436
01:17:11,655 --> 01:17:14,321
Even when the high attack
or toss was not stable,

1437
01:17:14,321 --> 01:17:16,355
Yoon Young In managed
to land a powerful attack.

1438
01:17:16,355 --> 01:17:19,921
Lee Na-Yeon's toss was
also picture-perfect.

1439
01:17:19,921 --> 01:17:21,503
She set the ball right on target,

1440
01:17:21,855 --> 01:17:23,388
and the spike was flawless.

1441
01:17:24,721 --> 01:17:28,521
(Never been on the pro team,)

1442
01:17:29,488 --> 01:17:32,655
(Yoon Young In has been the player
of a corporate team for eight years.)

1443
01:17:33,288 --> 01:17:37,121
(Although she made a hurried retreat,)

1444
01:17:38,421 --> 01:17:42,121
(Lee Na-Yeon, the retired player,
starts again with sincerity alone.)

1445
01:17:43,788 --> 01:17:44,821
Let's have fun!

1446
01:17:44,821 --> 01:17:46,321
Laugh and chat!

1447
01:17:48,288 --> 01:17:51,921
I loved working together
with my teammates.

1448
01:17:51,921 --> 01:17:53,755
I thought that volleyball is...

1449
01:17:54,321 --> 01:17:59,188
something I can never let go
even if I wanted to.

1450
01:17:59,788 --> 01:18:02,521
I was happy and welled up.

1451
01:18:04,088 --> 01:18:05,655
You're getting teary.

1452
01:18:07,121 --> 01:18:10,188
I got rid of lots
of uncomfortable memories.

1453
01:18:10,188 --> 01:18:12,488
The game is no longer stressful.

1454
01:18:12,988 --> 01:18:14,221
It's fun.

1455
01:18:14,788 --> 01:18:17,088
Na-Yeon!

1456
01:18:17,088 --> 01:18:18,088
(Raising her thumb)

1457
01:18:18,521 --> 01:18:19,555
Keep that up.

1458
01:18:20,321 --> 01:18:21,921
(Na-Yeon is more confident
about her toss.)

1459
01:18:22,221 --> 01:18:23,355
From the left!

1460
01:18:24,021 --> 01:18:25,010
It's a block-out.

1461
01:18:25,035 --> 01:18:26,955
They've got the momentum. It's 18 to 16.

1462
01:18:31,888 --> 01:18:33,788
A back-row attack from the middle!

1463
01:18:33,788 --> 01:18:35,288
It's inside the court!

1464
01:18:36,155 --> 01:18:40,288
(The atmosphere on the court lights up
with the setter.)

1465
01:18:41,555 --> 01:18:43,255
I couldn't help but smile.

1466
01:18:43,255 --> 01:18:45,988
I knew I was right.

1467
01:18:46,288 --> 01:18:50,787
The more the setter gains confidence,
the less restraint she has...

1468
01:18:50,811 --> 01:18:53,621
and the more she can play
in her own style.

1469
01:18:53,621 --> 01:18:57,555
It would be a huge challenge
for Geunyoung Girls' High.

1470
01:19:00,655 --> 01:19:01,688
Should I press it?

1471
01:19:03,221 --> 01:19:07,921
(Time-out for Geunyoung Girls' High)

1472
01:19:09,121 --> 01:19:11,821
(Grave)

1473
01:19:12,521 --> 01:19:16,121
(The atmosphere turns tense.)

1474
01:19:16,121 --> 01:19:18,421
You're not observing the setter at all.

1475
01:19:18,988 --> 01:19:21,688
If you just go for the angle and attack,

1476
01:19:21,688 --> 01:19:24,588
- they will obviously be ready to block.
- Understood.

1477
01:19:24,588 --> 01:19:25,855
It's not a matter of losing a point.

1478
01:19:25,855 --> 01:19:28,221
- You need to take control first.
- Okay.

1479
01:19:28,221 --> 01:19:29,855
- Isn't it right?
- Yes.

1480
01:19:30,188 --> 01:19:32,321
- You know you can do it.
- Yes!

1481
01:19:32,321 --> 01:19:33,555
Geunyoung!

1482
01:19:35,321 --> 01:19:38,821
(Geunyoung Girls' High must
take back control,)

1483
01:19:39,688 --> 01:19:43,588
(while Wonder Dogs has to maintain it.)

1484
01:19:44,488 --> 01:19:48,055
(Yoon Young In serves.)

1485
01:19:54,321 --> 01:19:56,521
(Kim Yoon Ha's powerful spike)

1486
01:19:56,521 --> 01:19:57,555
(She fails to defend.)

1487
01:20:00,188 --> 01:20:01,355
Sorry!

1488
01:20:01,355 --> 01:20:04,255
(Their opposing team scores
after the time-out.)

1489
01:20:04,255 --> 01:20:06,855
Geunyoung Girls' High doesn't miss
their opportunity.

1490
01:20:07,355 --> 01:20:09,555
Kim Yoon Ha's hard spike worked!

1491
01:20:09,555 --> 01:20:10,555
Way to go!

1492
01:20:12,421 --> 01:20:14,988
(Geunyoung Girls' High serves.)

1493
01:20:16,388 --> 01:20:19,221
(They have the chance to strike back.)

1494
01:20:21,321 --> 01:20:23,088
That was a sharp serve,
and the reception goes unstable.

1495
01:20:25,055 --> 01:20:26,155
(She saves the ball.)

1496
01:20:26,155 --> 01:20:28,321
The ball flies, and she spikes high!

1497
01:20:28,321 --> 01:20:30,255
(Back Chae-Rim's spike)

1498
01:20:31,021 --> 01:20:34,288
(The mood changes right away.)

1499
01:20:34,588 --> 01:20:35,988
(Happy)

1500
01:20:35,988 --> 01:20:37,921
(Gloomy)

1501
01:20:38,588 --> 01:20:40,621
(Geunyoung Girls' High attempts
to counterattack.)

1502
01:20:40,621 --> 01:20:43,188
(But they make an error.)

1503
01:20:45,288 --> 01:20:47,655
(Another error)

1504
01:20:50,755 --> 01:20:51,955
(Making a third error)

1505
01:20:52,255 --> 01:20:56,221
(The mood completely shifts
to Wonder Dogs.)

1506
01:20:56,955 --> 01:20:58,588
It's 24 to 19.

1507
01:20:58,588 --> 01:21:01,021
Wonder Dogs are at the set point
in the first set.

1508
01:21:01,621 --> 01:21:05,088
- Just one more!
- One more point!

1509
01:21:05,488 --> 01:21:10,088
(They only have one point left
to win the first set.)

1510
01:21:10,421 --> 01:21:12,621
Don't quit. It's not over yet!

1511
01:21:12,621 --> 01:21:13,855
(Keeping in check)

1512
01:21:14,788 --> 01:21:17,688
Check where number 4 goes, Enkhsoyol.

1513
01:21:19,155 --> 01:21:23,121
(Na-Yeon instructs the plan to Enkhsoyol.)

1514
01:21:23,121 --> 01:21:25,055
- Number 17 is at the front.
- Okay.

1515
01:21:25,355 --> 01:21:29,088
(The fate of the two teams is
in a single point.)

1516
01:21:29,088 --> 01:21:32,621
(Wonder Dogs' set point)

1517
01:21:33,288 --> 01:21:34,321
Serve!

1518
01:21:34,321 --> 01:21:36,888
(Kim Yoon Ha serves.)

1519
01:21:39,955 --> 01:21:41,088
The ball goes up!

1520
01:21:41,088 --> 01:21:42,121
(Enkhsoyol spikes hard.)

1521
01:21:42,555 --> 01:21:44,255
(Super dig)

1522
01:21:46,155 --> 01:21:48,055
- They were able to defend.
- Yes. They did.

1523
01:21:51,260 --> 01:21:52,588
(A free ball)

1524
01:21:52,588 --> 01:21:54,588
She spikes one more time!

1525
01:21:54,588 --> 01:21:56,555
(She succeeds to spike.)

1526
01:21:57,355 --> 01:21:59,821
(We won the first set!)

1527
01:21:59,821 --> 01:22:01,355
It's 25 to 19.

1528
01:22:01,355 --> 01:22:03,888
Wonder Dogs takes the first set.

1529
01:22:05,188 --> 01:22:06,621
You did great!

1530
01:22:06,621 --> 01:22:10,288
(The new head coach finally smiles.)

1531
01:22:14,088 --> 01:22:16,855
I was so proud of them
as their head coach.

1532
01:22:18,088 --> 01:22:21,688
I felt that I could say,
"Our players are not that weak!"

1533
01:22:21,688 --> 01:22:26,955
The training was really helpful
for the players.

1534
01:22:26,955 --> 01:22:28,988
But due to our errors,

1535
01:22:28,988 --> 01:22:32,555
we had to give points
to our opposing team.

1536
01:22:32,555 --> 01:22:35,355
So, as a head coach, I wondered
how to solve this...

1537
01:22:35,355 --> 01:22:39,988
so that the players can adapt quickly.

1538
01:22:40,688 --> 01:22:43,355
Wonder Dogs takes the first set!

1539
01:22:45,888 --> 01:22:49,088
(Time-out for the second set)

1540
01:22:49,955 --> 01:22:52,788
Myoung-Hwa can go in the second set.

1541
01:22:52,788 --> 01:22:54,488
(Moon Myoung-Hwa as number 3?)

1542
01:22:54,888 --> 01:22:57,288
(On the volleyball court,)

1543
01:22:57,955 --> 01:23:00,555
(each position has its own number.)

1544
01:23:00,555 --> 01:23:03,388
(The head coach decides
the positions for every set!)

1545
01:23:04,255 --> 01:23:08,888
(To strengthen the defense, in number 3,)

1546
01:23:09,521 --> 01:23:11,721
(Moon Myoung-Hwa, with a height
of 189cm, is positioned.)

1547
01:23:11,721 --> 01:23:13,721
(Reliable)

1548
01:23:16,321 --> 01:23:19,221
Cover number 17 when number 1
goes to the right.

1549
01:23:22,788 --> 01:23:24,321
(Second set, Geunyoung Girls' High 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

1550
01:23:24,346 --> 01:23:26,680
The second set begins
with Enkhsoyol's serve.

1551
01:23:27,021 --> 01:23:28,155
Serve!

1552
01:23:28,155 --> 01:23:31,955
(Enkhsoyol serves.)

1553
01:23:33,488 --> 01:23:34,921
Making an underhand toss.

1554
01:23:36,521 --> 01:23:38,488
(Blocking)

1555
01:23:38,488 --> 01:23:39,688
She saves, and then Lee Na-Yeon!

1556
01:23:41,155 --> 01:23:42,155
It's a back attack!

1557
01:23:42,988 --> 01:23:44,055
The ball goes up.

1558
01:23:44,521 --> 01:23:45,655
Oh Eun Chae.

1559
01:23:48,088 --> 01:23:49,888
(They score by blocking.)

1560
01:23:49,888 --> 01:23:52,588
The presence of Moon Myoung-Hwa
does matter.

1561
01:23:52,588 --> 01:23:53,755
You're right.

1562
01:23:55,355 --> 01:23:57,088
Nice blocking, Myoung-Hwa.

1563
01:23:57,848 --> 01:23:59,921
- Nice Blocking.
- Great defense!

1564
01:24:00,821 --> 01:24:03,388
The team is off to a good start
with solid blocking.

1565
01:24:03,388 --> 01:24:04,455
They get the point first.

1566
01:24:05,855 --> 01:24:06,888
It's soft.

1567
01:24:09,160 --> 01:24:10,346
A strong spike!

1568
01:24:11,113 --> 01:24:12,137
She tossed it up.

1569
01:24:12,685 --> 01:24:13,519
Come on.

1570
01:24:14,824 --> 01:24:16,824
(A mis-hit)

1571
01:24:18,119 --> 01:24:18,986
Sorry.

1572
01:24:19,845 --> 01:24:22,079
(Na-Yeon's setting error)

1573
01:24:22,712 --> 01:24:23,512
Sorry.

1574
01:24:23,845 --> 01:24:25,045
Let's try again.

1575
01:24:27,809 --> 01:24:29,979
When they make a bad set,

1576
01:24:29,979 --> 01:24:33,912
they have to get over it
and move on to the next play.

1577
01:24:34,226 --> 01:24:35,626
It's 1 to 1.

1578
01:24:35,626 --> 01:24:36,626
Serve!

1579
01:24:41,193 --> 01:24:42,659
(Straight out of court)

1580
01:24:42,659 --> 01:24:43,859
It's out.

1581
01:24:45,259 --> 01:24:47,026
(Frustrated)

1582
01:24:47,026 --> 01:24:50,893
Losing the opening set
in a reversal clearly took...

1583
01:24:50,893 --> 01:24:53,959
- the wind out of Geunyoung Girls' High.
- Yes, definitely.

1584
01:24:54,593 --> 01:24:56,559
(This could be our chance.)

1585
01:24:57,926 --> 01:24:58,826
Myoung-Hwa!

1586
01:24:59,393 --> 01:25:00,593
Try this play.

1587
01:25:00,593 --> 01:25:01,793
(Giving the serving instruction)

1588
01:25:06,126 --> 01:25:07,993
(Target area)

1589
01:25:12,719 --> 01:25:14,619
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

1590
01:25:16,326 --> 01:25:18,093
(Serve hits the spot!)

1591
01:25:20,226 --> 01:25:21,093
I'll get it!

1592
01:25:22,893 --> 01:25:24,359
Ace serve!

1593
01:25:25,659 --> 01:25:28,459
(The strategy worked perfectly.)

1594
01:25:28,759 --> 01:25:30,759
Myoung-Hwa owns the second set.

1595
01:25:32,226 --> 01:25:33,726
That was amazing!

1596
01:25:33,726 --> 01:25:35,226
Block and serve!

1597
01:25:36,293 --> 01:25:37,159
Amazing!

1598
01:25:38,459 --> 01:25:40,759
(Myoung-Hwa's serve)

1599
01:25:42,259 --> 01:25:43,159
Myoung-Hwa.

1600
01:25:46,059 --> 01:25:48,693
(Target serve to zone three)

1601
01:25:52,393 --> 01:25:53,326
Oh, man!

1602
01:25:56,152 --> 01:25:58,886
(Serve missed the target zone.)

1603
01:26:01,993 --> 01:26:03,126
Is it crossing the net?

1604
01:26:03,126 --> 01:26:04,326
They kept it alive.

1605
01:26:04,326 --> 01:26:05,159
Attack!

1606
01:26:06,393 --> 01:26:08,126
Strong hit from Yoo Da Eun!

1607
01:26:08,893 --> 01:26:11,126
Yoo Da Eun and Kim Yoon Ha's...

1608
01:26:11,126 --> 01:26:14,293
attacking duo is proving very effective.

1609
01:26:14,633 --> 01:26:16,866
I gave Myoung-Hwa a signal,
but she hit it short to the middle.

1610
01:26:17,259 --> 01:26:18,126
It was a serving error.

1611
01:26:18,126 --> 01:26:20,826
- I told you to hit Zone three.
- I know, but I missed.

1612
01:26:28,693 --> 01:26:29,559
Serve.

1613
01:26:30,226 --> 01:26:31,759
It is now three to two.

1614
01:26:36,893 --> 01:26:39,159
They failed to receive and lost a point.

1615
01:26:39,859 --> 01:26:40,793
Three to three.

1616
01:26:40,793 --> 01:26:43,026
Geunyoung Girls' High School caught up.

1617
01:26:43,026 --> 01:26:45,726
Wait for it. Don't rush.

1618
01:26:45,726 --> 01:26:47,059
They're not so fast.

1619
01:26:48,159 --> 01:26:49,159
Serve.

1620
01:26:53,959 --> 01:26:54,826
That's it.
Nice pass.

1621
01:26:56,659 --> 01:26:58,893
- Mine!
- Oh, no!

1622
01:26:58,893 --> 01:27:00,059
The ball is out!

1623
01:27:00,059 --> 01:27:01,159
(Out)

1624
01:27:01,693 --> 01:27:03,693
No touch.

1625
01:27:03,693 --> 01:27:06,126
- They called it out.
- Yes, correct.

1626
01:27:07,026 --> 01:27:08,493
(It was a touch.)

1627
01:27:12,993 --> 01:27:14,593
She's requesting a video challenge.

1628
01:27:14,658 --> 01:27:15,678
(It was a touch.)

1629
01:27:15,726 --> 01:27:17,693
One of a coach's key skills...

1630
01:27:17,693 --> 01:27:20,326
- is knowing when to call for...
- Yes, a video review.

1631
01:27:20,326 --> 01:27:21,593
Video challenge.

1632
01:27:21,593 --> 01:27:22,893
It looked like there was a touch.

1633
01:27:24,559 --> 01:27:26,126
(The Wonder Coach is confident.)

1634
01:27:26,126 --> 01:27:27,093
- What?
- No?

1635
01:27:27,093 --> 01:27:29,059
- Seemed so to me.
- I thought it was a no-touch.

1636
01:27:29,059 --> 01:27:30,459
Really? We'll find out soon.

1637
01:27:33,293 --> 01:27:35,526
That's Yoo Da Eun.

1638
01:27:36,526 --> 01:27:40,593
The attack went
right through the two blockers.

1639
01:27:41,826 --> 01:27:44,726
(Staring at the screen)

1640
01:27:46,326 --> 01:27:49,426
(It was a no-touch!)

1641
01:27:49,893 --> 01:27:50,759
After review,

1642
01:27:50,759 --> 01:27:56,693
It wasn't a touch-out.

1643
01:27:58,026 --> 01:27:58,926
Damn it.

1644
01:27:59,659 --> 01:28:01,493
They confirmed it wasn't a touch-out.

1645
01:28:01,493 --> 01:28:03,993
Calling for a video review
isn't an easy job for a coach.

1646
01:28:03,993 --> 01:28:05,093
- When you're playing,
- Of course.

1647
01:28:05,093 --> 01:28:06,659
you can say...

1648
01:28:06,659 --> 01:28:09,626
whatever you think you saw
and insist on it,

1649
01:28:09,626 --> 01:28:11,826
but a coach needs to make a call.

1650
01:28:13,226 --> 01:28:15,959
(The Wonder Dogs lost their lead.)

1651
01:28:19,126 --> 01:28:20,459
Nice pass by Enkhsoyol.

1652
01:28:22,859 --> 01:28:24,993
(The Wonder Dogs caught up!)

1653
01:28:25,793 --> 01:28:26,993
Nice work.

1654
01:28:26,993 --> 01:28:27,926
(Second set, Geunyoung Girls' High 4
: Wonder Dogs 4)

1655
01:28:29,193 --> 01:28:30,259
Tossed high into the air.

1656
01:28:31,193 --> 01:28:32,859
Powerful hit in the middle!

1657
01:28:33,526 --> 01:28:36,726
(Geunyoung Girls' High
quickly regained the lead, 5 to 4.)

1658
01:28:37,593 --> 01:28:39,259
Back-row attack, on the move!

1659
01:28:39,259 --> 01:28:40,493
They scored a point.

1660
01:28:40,493 --> 01:28:44,093
I think that was
their first back-row attack of the day.

1661
01:28:46,326 --> 01:28:47,893
(Jung Sol Min's diving dig)

1662
01:28:47,893 --> 01:28:48,893
Diving dig!

1663
01:28:51,826 --> 01:28:53,526
- Look.
- They're passing.

1664
01:28:53,526 --> 01:28:55,826
They're passing it around,
then a powerful spike!

1665
01:28:56,526 --> 01:28:57,393
Go!

1666
01:28:58,659 --> 01:29:01,226
(Is it our point?)

1667
01:29:01,426 --> 01:29:02,459
Go!

1668
01:29:07,593 --> 01:29:09,626
(Unbelievable dig to keep it in play)

1669
01:29:11,526 --> 01:29:13,493
Jung Da Eun hits it, and it's going over.

1670
01:29:13,493 --> 01:29:14,393
It's going over!

1671
01:29:16,259 --> 01:29:17,226
Unbelievable save!

1672
01:29:18,626 --> 01:29:21,126
The rally's getting longer.
What a scramble.

1673
01:29:21,126 --> 01:29:22,193
(Someone needs to end this.)

1674
01:29:22,826 --> 01:29:24,993
Another powerful strike from the wing!

1675
01:29:25,093 --> 01:29:27,026
- Nice attack.
- Point for the Wonder Dogs.

1676
01:29:27,026 --> 01:29:28,626
(Rise high, Wonder Dogs!)

1677
01:29:28,626 --> 01:29:29,659
Nice work!

1678
01:29:29,659 --> 01:29:31,726
- Nice.
- We're doing great.

1679
01:29:31,726 --> 01:29:34,493
(Wonder Dogs leading, seven to eight)

1680
01:29:35,493 --> 01:29:36,993
That was an amazing play.

1681
01:29:37,434 --> 01:29:41,601
Both teams deserve applause
for that rally.

1682
01:29:41,626 --> 01:29:43,159
Yes, it was a mega-rally.

1683
01:29:43,526 --> 01:29:46,893
I really thought Geunyoung Girls' High
wouldn't be able to return it.

1684
01:29:47,726 --> 01:29:48,693
Look right there.

1685
01:29:50,126 --> 01:29:51,426
I can't believe she saved that.

1686
01:29:52,393 --> 01:29:54,626
(The undisputed ace, Jung Sol Min)

1687
01:29:54,626 --> 01:29:55,826
Nice work, Sol Min.

1688
01:29:57,393 --> 01:29:59,059
Let's do this.

1689
01:29:59,426 --> 01:30:01,293
(So charismatic)

1690
01:30:01,593 --> 01:30:03,326
(In the next rally...)

1691
01:30:03,793 --> 01:30:08,159
A direct kill!

1692
01:30:09,026 --> 01:30:10,226
Sorry.

1693
01:30:10,826 --> 01:30:12,059
- Yes!
- Nice job!

1694
01:30:12,059 --> 01:30:13,859
They seized the opportunity.

1695
01:30:14,093 --> 01:30:15,210
It's tied at 8 to 8.

1696
01:30:16,093 --> 01:30:17,379
They're setting it up...

1697
01:30:17,859 --> 01:30:19,381
and going for a back-row attack!

1698
01:30:19,559 --> 01:30:22,559
(Jin Soo Min's hustle play)

1699
01:30:24,326 --> 01:30:26,026
A pass, then a surprise tip.

1700
01:30:26,026 --> 01:30:27,026
(A surprise tip)

1701
01:30:27,593 --> 01:30:29,459
- Oh, no.
- Lost the point.

1702
01:30:29,893 --> 01:30:31,326
Back on top, 9 to 8.

1703
01:30:32,159 --> 01:30:33,826
All right, you're doing great!

1704
01:30:33,826 --> 01:30:35,493
(Neck and neck, only one point apart)

1705
01:30:35,493 --> 01:30:36,393
Nice blocking!

1706
01:30:36,393 --> 01:30:39,693
Geunyoung Girls' High
kept catching up to us,

1707
01:30:39,693 --> 01:30:42,459
and I started to feel a bit rattled.

1708
01:30:42,459 --> 01:30:46,426
Many games are decided
by just one or two points.

1709
01:30:46,426 --> 01:30:49,093
We call that a one-point game.

1710
01:30:49,093 --> 01:30:53,493
I believe that one point is decided
by the smallest details.

1711
01:30:54,126 --> 01:30:56,126
What should I do at this point?

1712
01:30:56,726 --> 01:31:00,226
I kept thinking about that
while I was watching.

1713
01:31:01,593 --> 01:31:02,526
They passed it.

1714
01:31:03,759 --> 01:31:05,193
Another powerful strike!

1715
01:31:05,193 --> 01:31:07,193
- A successful block!
- Nice blocking.

1716
01:31:07,193 --> 01:31:08,726
(Another point lost)

1717
01:31:10,959 --> 01:31:11,959
Enkhsoyol.

1718
01:31:11,959 --> 01:31:13,793
Geunyoung Girls' High scores on the block!

1719
01:31:13,793 --> 01:31:15,793
Back-to-back blocks
by Geunyoung Girls' High.

1720
01:31:16,159 --> 01:31:17,626
Nice blocks, girls.

1721
01:31:19,393 --> 01:31:24,026
It seems like
the Wonder Dogs need to know that,

1722
01:31:24,026 --> 01:31:27,126
in this kind of ongoing rally game,

1723
01:31:27,126 --> 01:31:30,926
they need to stabilize
their connections a bit.

1724
01:31:30,926 --> 01:31:32,093
(They have to regain control.)

1725
01:31:32,326 --> 01:31:36,559
It occurred to me that today's game
might be quite challenging.

1726
01:31:36,559 --> 01:31:40,026
I wanted to do something
to help the players...

1727
01:31:40,426 --> 01:31:42,826
and I thought they needed a wake-up call.

1728
01:31:42,826 --> 01:31:44,626
(Something has to be done!)

1729
01:31:45,259 --> 01:31:46,926
Myoung-Hwa, move in advance.

1730
01:31:47,659 --> 01:31:49,093
Let's do this, girls.

1731
01:31:49,893 --> 01:31:51,593
Nice positioning, Young In.

1732
01:31:53,359 --> 01:31:54,959
(Is she simply checking their positions?)

1733
01:31:55,326 --> 01:31:58,026
(Or is this a strategy
by the Wonder Coach?)

1734
01:31:58,459 --> 01:32:00,859
(Enkhsoyol's serve)

1735
01:32:03,559 --> 01:32:06,026
(An offensive opportunity
for Geunyoung Girls' High)

1736
01:32:06,859 --> 01:32:09,593
Myoung-Hwa blocked the ball!

1737
01:32:09,593 --> 01:32:11,359
Moon Myoung-Hwa!

1738
01:32:11,359 --> 01:32:12,359
(A perfect defense)

1739
01:32:13,126 --> 01:32:14,259
In the second set,

1740
01:32:14,259 --> 01:32:16,926
the Wonder Dogs got a point off a block.

1741
01:32:16,926 --> 01:32:20,659
They made it seem like
they were covering the line,

1742
01:32:20,659 --> 01:32:22,359
but Young In redirected it.

1743
01:32:22,359 --> 01:32:24,926
As far as I know, Coach Yeon Koung...

1744
01:32:24,926 --> 01:32:26,859
actually came up
with this tactic beforehand.

1745
01:32:27,159 --> 01:32:29,159
Nice one, Young In.

1746
01:32:30,193 --> 01:32:32,059
Great positioning for the block.

1747
01:32:32,626 --> 01:32:35,593
Most of their offense is going
through the left side.

1748
01:32:35,993 --> 01:32:39,026
So we can use a trick.
Make it seem like we're guarding the line,

1749
01:32:39,659 --> 01:32:42,226
but where do we really block?

1750
01:32:42,226 --> 01:32:43,493
In between.

1751
01:32:44,059 --> 01:32:45,926
(Just like Coach Yeon Koung's tactic,)

1752
01:32:45,926 --> 01:32:48,026
(she moved her spot a bit...)

1753
01:32:48,393 --> 01:32:49,493
(and successfully blocked the ball.)

1754
01:32:49,826 --> 01:32:52,034
Our goal for this game is...

1755
01:32:52,059 --> 01:32:55,226
to finish this game
without the opponent knowing our tactic.

1756
01:32:55,893 --> 01:32:57,926
(Right after her attack was blocked,)

1757
01:32:58,826 --> 01:33:00,993
(the opponent looks shaken.)

1758
01:33:00,993 --> 01:33:02,326
Sorry.

1759
01:33:02,326 --> 01:33:03,693
(This is what I'm talking about.)

1760
01:33:04,126 --> 01:33:09,193
(The score is now 12 to 13,
advantage Wonder Dogs)

1761
01:33:09,626 --> 01:33:10,659
Serve!

1762
01:33:10,659 --> 01:33:11,659
Kim Yoon Ha to serve.

1763
01:33:12,493 --> 01:33:13,559
One, two, three.

1764
01:33:14,859 --> 01:33:16,493
That was a tough pass.

1765
01:33:18,259 --> 01:33:19,459
(A super powerful spike!)

1766
01:33:19,459 --> 01:33:20,826
She hit it cross-court.

1767
01:33:21,493 --> 01:33:22,559
They saved it.

1768
01:33:24,359 --> 01:33:25,859
Block!

1769
01:33:25,859 --> 01:33:27,826
(Back-to-back blocking points)

1770
01:33:29,593 --> 01:33:31,226
Point for us again!

1771
01:33:31,759 --> 01:33:33,059
(The coach's tactic is working.)

1772
01:33:33,059 --> 01:33:34,175
That was amazing.

1773
01:33:34,693 --> 01:33:36,093
Myoung-Hwa is on fire!

1774
01:33:37,159 --> 01:33:40,593
(The blocking queen, Myoung-Hwa)

1775
01:33:41,326 --> 01:33:44,359
In her pro days, if I recall correctly,

1776
01:33:44,359 --> 01:33:49,826
Myoung-Hwa's record for the most blocks
in a game is seven.

1777
01:33:49,826 --> 01:33:52,893
And she's already blocked three
in today's game.

1778
01:33:52,893 --> 01:33:55,859
Myoung-Hwa is on a blocking roll.

1779
01:33:55,859 --> 01:33:58,226
(It's a blocking party out here.)

1780
01:33:59,926 --> 01:34:02,726
It was such a rush.

1781
01:34:02,726 --> 01:34:06,626
Every time I felt lost about how to block,

1782
01:34:06,626 --> 01:34:08,493
the coach gave me solutions.

1783
01:34:08,493 --> 01:34:09,426
Detailed solutions.

1784
01:34:09,426 --> 01:34:11,650
Such as, "Get the timing right."

1785
01:34:11,650 --> 01:34:13,750
Don't rush it. Wait.

1786
01:34:13,750 --> 01:34:14,451
She tells me where to look.

1787
01:34:14,475 --> 01:34:15,983
Look at my fingers.

1788
01:34:16,250 --> 01:34:19,850
(The rookie coach encourages them
to keep at it.)

1789
01:34:20,150 --> 01:34:23,350
She gives us effective advice.

1790
01:34:24,683 --> 01:34:31,083
(To some,
Moon Myoung-Hwa might seem slow.)

1791
01:34:32,817 --> 01:34:34,550
(But today,)

1792
01:34:35,317 --> 01:34:39,283
(she's the nimblest on the court.)

1793
01:34:39,283 --> 01:34:40,150
Myoung-Hwa.

1794
01:34:40,150 --> 01:34:42,083
(Thumbs up for the quick Myoung-Hwa.)

1795
01:34:42,550 --> 01:34:43,750
Great job, Myoung-Hwa.

1796
01:34:48,917 --> 01:34:53,383
(A serve from Myoung-Hwa,
the rookie blocker.)

1797
01:34:55,917 --> 01:34:57,017
Nice serve.

1798
01:34:58,850 --> 01:35:01,083
(Another successful block?)

1799
01:35:01,083 --> 01:35:02,083
Hit it!

1800
01:35:02,083 --> 01:35:03,117
It drops to the right.

1801
01:35:06,643 --> 01:35:10,943
(An impenetrable wall of single block.)

1802
01:35:12,650 --> 01:35:15,850
(Wonder Dogs never tumble down.)

1803
01:35:15,983 --> 01:35:23,083
The energetic play and teamwork
are leading to scores!

1804
01:35:23,083 --> 01:35:26,883
The Wonder Dogs' blocking
is amazing in the second set!

1805
01:35:28,950 --> 01:35:32,150
(Dumbfounded)

1806
01:35:32,517 --> 01:35:33,650
It's okay.

1807
01:35:33,650 --> 01:35:35,850
- I'm sorry.
- It's alright.

1808
01:35:36,792 --> 01:35:39,358
Young In, get closer to the net.

1809
01:35:39,383 --> 01:35:42,450
Wait at the front
and go for it at the end.

1810
01:35:47,250 --> 01:35:50,350
(Wonder Dogs' "sheriff,"
Moon Myoung-Hwa, serves.)

1811
01:35:54,383 --> 01:35:56,117
(Another one?)

1812
01:35:56,395 --> 01:35:58,283
It's left this time. Will it score?

1813
01:36:00,550 --> 01:36:01,817
(Consecutive blocking scores)

1814
01:36:01,817 --> 01:36:03,517
It's another point!

1815
01:36:05,583 --> 01:36:09,483
(It's a party now!)

1816
01:36:10,350 --> 01:36:11,283
Gosh!

1817
01:36:13,083 --> 01:36:15,517
The Geunyoung Girls' High needs to know...

1818
01:36:15,517 --> 01:36:18,117
that the Wonder Dog players at the side...

1819
01:36:18,117 --> 01:36:21,350
are sending their blocks to the center.

1820
01:36:21,350 --> 01:36:26,750
But Geunyoung Girls' High's spikes
are all aiming at the middle!

1821
01:36:26,750 --> 01:36:28,517
How many blocks did they get?

1822
01:36:28,517 --> 01:36:31,850
The Wonder Dogs are blocking everything
in the second set!

1823
01:36:32,150 --> 01:36:34,517
I can see that our players...

1824
01:36:34,517 --> 01:36:38,017
understood and carried out the plan.

1825
01:36:38,017 --> 01:36:41,550
The successes give me a thrill.

1826
01:36:41,783 --> 01:36:42,750
I'm so proud of them.

1827
01:36:43,783 --> 01:36:47,217
Coach Kim's debut match only starts now!

1828
01:36:47,242 --> 01:36:48,222
(Let's get it started!)
